{"raw": {"https://towson.taleo.net/careersection/fac_ex/jobdetail.ftl?job=260000JS": {"title": "Collection Management Librarian", "description": "Job Description - Collection Management Librarian (260000JS) Go to the main content section. Welcome.  You are not signed in.  NOTE: If you experience any issues with this page, please contact the Towson University Office of Human Resources at 410-704-2162. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Collection Management Librarian (260000JS) Job Description Collection Management Librarian - ( 260000JS ) TU Search Number : LIB-4012 Librarian I or Librarian II Content Management Department Albert S. Cook Library LIB-4012 Towson University: Towson University (TU) is one of the nation\u2019s top 100 public universities. Located north of Baltimore, TU currently enrolls over 19,000 students and is the second-largest university in the prestigious University System of Maryland. Towson University fosters a climate that is grounded in respect to cultivate the intellectual and personal growth of the entire university community. Position: The Albert S. Cook Library invites applications for a Librarian I position in the Content Management Department. Preferred start date November 4, 2026. Under the general direction of the Director of Content Management, the Collection Management Librarian will provide flexible, responsive leadership in the management of collection development and acquisitions operation, including serving as the primary liaison contact for acquisitions operation. Leads the collection development team of librarians across departments, collaborating with the Director of Content Management and Head of Resource Sharing, to set group agendas, priorities and decision points for collection development. Formulates, develops, recommends and modifies policies and procedures for acquisitions as well as general library policies that involve acquisitions. Participates in library assessment initiatives. Required Qualifications: Librarian I: Master\u2019s degree in library or information science from an ALA-accredited institution or equivalent, or completion of a master\u2019s degree in library or information science within a year of the start date. Familiarity with library collection development, technical services, acquisitions, or other related library areas. Strong, positive interpersonal and collaborative skills; ability to work in a team environment. Excellent oral, written, and interpersonal communication skills. Ability to work flexibly and creatively in a changing and fast paced environment with a diverse population. Commitment to continued growth in areas of responsibility. Demonstrated ability to meet the University\u2019s criteria for promotion and permanent status of library faculty, through professional development and service accomplishments. Librarian II: In addition to the above, at least three years of professional experience as a librarian. Evidence of substantive contributions to the maintenance of quality in library services and resources. Documentation of successful completion of significant projects for a local, regional or national library or library association. Evidence of progress towards a scholarly research agenda including plan for publications, grants, evidence synthesis, creative works, etc. Evidence of service to prior library or campus including participation on committees; or evidence of participation on regional or national library associations. Preferred Qualifications: Knowledge of library acquisitions operations in a library environment. Experience administering the GOBI ordering platform. Demonstrated competencies as outlined in \u201cCore Competencies for Acquisitions Professionals\u201d (https://alair.ala.org/items/b1d2eac1-3493-427d-9c25-4399c7116a15) Demonstrated initiative and ability to work independently and collaboratively on a variety of projects simultaneously. Experience managing statistical data and generating reports. Familiarity with web discovery services, link resolvers, proxy and authentication services. Demonstrated initiative and ability to work independently and collaboratively on a variety of projects simultaneously. Demonstrated excellent organizational, analytical, time management, and project management skills. Ability to learn new library and computer technology and stay current with technology developments. Responsibilities: Under the general direction of the Director of Content Management, the Collection Management Librarian will provide flexible, responsive leadership in the management of collection development and acquisitions operation, including serving as the primary liaison contact for acquisitions operation. Leads the collection development team of librarians across departments, collaborating with the Director of Content Management and Head of Resource Sharing, to set group agendas, priorities and decision points for collection development. Formulates, develops, recommends and modifies policies and procedures for acquisitions as well as general library policies that involve acquisitions. Participates in library assessment initiatives. Provides leadership and oversight for the strategic growth, stewardship, and fiscal accountability of the library's collections. This role chairs or co-chairs collection development activities and works closely with the Director of Content Management, Head of Resource Sharing, and subject liaison librarians to coordinate selection and deselection decisions, establish approval plans, and ensure collections align with institutional priorities and user needs. The incumbent serves as a primary resource for librarians engaged in collection building, providing guidance and training on selection tools such as GOBI, evaluating collection funding and allocation models, and supporting data-informed decision-making regarding print and electronic resources. The position also collaborates on financial analyses related to transformative agreements, publisher pricing changes, and enrollment-driven funding needs to support budget planning and advocacy efforts. In addition, the position oversees acquisitions operations and promotes effective collaboration across library departments. Responsibilities include ensuring compliance with audit standards through accurate reconciliation and documentation of all library material purchases, developing and refining acquisitions policies and procedures, assessing workflows, and directing staff priorities to maximize efficiency and accountability. The incumbent manages systems supporting monograph selection and ordering, evaluates and implements acquisitions technologies, and analyzes data from library and vendor platforms to monitor performance and improve processes. Working closely with library unit leads and cross-functional teams, the position develops, documents, and communicates workflows that span multiple functional areas, fostering collaboration, consistency, and service excellence across the organization. The Department: Albert S. Cook Library is the campus library for Towson University, the largest university in the Baltimore area and the second largest in the University System of Maryland. Cook Library also serves the Towson University Northeastern Maryland (TUNE) campus. With 28 faculty librarians and 26 staff, Cook Library provides superior support to Towson University. Application Process: Review of applications begins immediately and continues until the position is filled. Applicant should submit a resume or curriculum vitae, cover letter, and the names and contact information of three relevant references. Click here to apply. Please note that the search number for which you are applying is LIB-4012. Please be sure to visit the Applicant Data Form to complete a voluntary on-line form. All data collected are for internal, state, and/or federal reporting and will not be used for other purposes. Organization : Academic Affairs Division Primary Location : Main Campus Job Posting : Aug 13, 2026 Towson University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. If you need a reasonable accommodation for any part of the employment process, please send an email to: adarequest@towson.edu Towson University is a smoke-free campus. \u00a92016 | 8000 York Road | Towson, MD 21252 | 410-704-2000"}, "https://towson.taleo.net/careersection/fac_ex/jobdetail.ftl?job=260000OM": {"title": "Assistant Professor in Finance", "description": "Job Description - Assistant Professor in Finance (260000OM) Go to the main content section. Welcome.  You are not signed in.  NOTE: If you experience any issues with this page, please contact the Towson University Office of Human Resources at 410-704-2162. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Assistant Professor in Finance (260000OM) Job Description Assistant Professor in Finance - ( 260000OM ) TU Search Number : CBE-4019 Towson University: Towson University (TU) is one of the nation\u2019s top 100 public universities. Located north of Baltimore, TU currently enrolls over 19,000 students and is the second-largest university in the prestigious University System of Maryland. Towson University fosters a climate that is grounded in respect to cultivate the intellectual and personal growth of the entire university community. Position: The College of Business and Economics invites applications for a tenure-track, 9-month Assistant Professor position in the Department of Finance beginning August 2027. Qualifications: PhD in Finance from an AACSB accredited institution. ABD applicants considered, but appointment will be at the Instructor rank and all degree requirements must be completed by August 1, 2027. A PhD in Financial Planning may be considered. Evidence of a strong commitment to teaching and mentoring students, promise of high-quality research, and the ability to work in a collaborative manner with colleagues and professional peers. Professional certifications such as the Chartered Financial Analyst (CFA) or the Certified Financial Planner (CFP) will be helpful. Industry experience is appreciated. Salary and Benefits: Targeted salary range: $150,000-$153,200 Benefits: TU offers a comprehensive benefits package that includes excellent health, life and retirement plans; and tuition remission. To learn more about our benefits, click here for regular faculty/regular lecturer or here for contingent lecturer. TU also offers a variety of great perks and discounts, which can be found here. For more information regarding this position and to view the ad in its entirety, we ask that you visit the Office of the Provost website and view our open faculty positions at https://www.towson.edu/provost/prospective/openpositions.html Organization : Academic Affairs Division Primary Location : Main Campus Job Posting : Sep 11, 2026 Towson University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. If you need a reasonable accommodation for any part of the employment process, please send an email to: adarequest@towson.edu Towson University is a smoke-free campus. \u00a92016 | 8000 York Road | Towson, MD 21252 | 410-704-2000"}, "https://towson.taleo.net/careersection/fac_ex/jobdetail.ftl?job=260000N7": {"title": "Assistant Professor- Department of Early Childhood Education", "description": "Job Description - Assistant Professor- Department of Early Childhood Education (260000N7) Go to the main content section. Welcome.  You are not signed in.  NOTE: If you experience any issues with this page, please contact the Towson University Office of Human Resources at 410-704-2162. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Assistant Professor- Department of Early Childhood Education (260000N7) Job Description Assistant Professor- Department of Early Childhood Education - ( 260000N7 ) TU Search Number : COE-4016 Assistant Professor Department of Early Childhood Education College of Education COE-4016 Towson University: Towson University (TU) is one of the nation\u2019s top 100 public universities. Located north of Baltimore, TU currently enrolls over 19,000 students and is the second-largest university in the prestigious University System of Maryland. Towson University fosters a climate that is grounded in respect to cultivate the intellectual and personal growth of the entire university community. Position: The College of Education invites applications for a n Assistant Professor position in the Department of Early Childhood Education. Preferred start date August 2027. Qualifications: \u00b7 Doctoral degree in early childhood education, reading and literacy, curriculum and instruction, teacher education, or related fields. \u00b7 ABD applicants with on-going progress will be considered if all degree requirements are completed by June 1, 2028. \u00b7 Commitment to excellence in teaching. \u00b7 Evidence of sustained commitment to working in partnership with public schools, children and families and/or other early childhood setting. \u00b7 Expertise in early literacy practices and/or Science of Reading. \u00b7 Demonstrated teaching experience in early literacy. \u00b7 Demonstrated success or potential to teach a wide variety of early childhood and/or gifted education courses at the undergraduate and graduate level. \u00b7 Evidence of strong potential for scholarly productivity, including research publications and conference presentations that are innovative, collaborative, or interdisciplinary. \u00b7 Three or more years\u2019 experience working in public schools, Head Start programs, and/or other early childhood settings. Responsibilities: Faculty will be assigned an instructional workload of six (6) course units per academic year, which may include supervising student interns off campus. Undergraduate advising is part of teaching responsibilities. Scholarly research productivity, programmatic assessment activity, and service to the department, college, and university are expected. Candidates may be asked to teach in person on campus and/or via online formats and may have additional duties based upon applicant qualifications and departmental needs. The Department: The Department of Early Childhood Education is distinguished nationally and regionally by its breadth, expertise and innovative practices. Towson University\u2019s College of Education has been a leader in teacher preparation for over 150 years, and its programs are recognized for their high quality and innovation. The programs in the Department of Early Childhood Education have been Nationally Recognized by National Association for the Education of Young Children (NAEYC). ECED offers an undergraduate program, a Master\u2019s of Education in Early Childhood Education, and a Master\u2019s of Education in Gifted and Creative Education (Pre-K-12). Application Process: Review of applications begins immediately and continues until the position is filled. Interested applicants should submit their CV, transcripts, three letters of recommendation and a letter of application describing qualifications. All applicants must apply through Taleo. Click here to apply. Please note that the search number for which you are applying is COE-3905. Please be sure to visit the Applicant Data Form to complete a voluntary online form. All data collected are for internal, state, and/or federal reporting and will not be used for other purposes. Click here to apply. Please note that the search number for which you are applying is COE-4016. Please be sure to visit the Applicant Data Form to complete a voluntary on-line form. All data collected are for internal, state, and/or federal reporting and will not be used for other purposes. Salary and Benefits: Targeted salary range: $70,000-$72,000 commensurate with experience. Benefits: TU offers a comprehensive benefits package that includes excellent health, life and retirement plans; and tuition remission. To learn more about our benefits, click here for regular faculty/regular lecturer or here for contingent lecturer. TU also offers a variety of great perks and discounts, which can be found here. Background Check: A Criminal Background Investigation is required for the hired candidate and the results may impact employment. COVID-19 Statement: The safety of our students, faculty, staff, and neighbors has been our top priority and the focus of every one of our decisions since the earliest days of the COVID-19 pandemic. Therefore, the University System of Maryland (USM) has strongly encouraged full COVID vaccination and up-to-date booster shots (when eligible) for all faculty, staff, and students at all schools in the USM as both a reasonable and necessary means of protecting our health and safety. Organization : Academic Affairs Division Primary Location : Main Campus Job Posting : Aug 26, 2026 Towson University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. If you need a reasonable accommodation for any part of the employment process, please send an email to: adarequest@towson.edu Towson University is a smoke-free campus. \u00a92016 | 8000 York Road | Towson, MD 21252 | 410-704-2000"}, "https://towson.taleo.net/careersection/fac_ex/jobdetail.ftl?job=260000QS": {"title": "Assistant Professor in Elementary Education", "description": "Job Description - Assistant Professor in Elementary Education (260000QS) Go to the main content section. Welcome.  You are not signed in.  NOTE: If you experience any issues with this page, please contact the Towson University Office of Human Resources at 410-704-2162. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Assistant Professor in Elementary Education (260000QS) Job Description Assistant Professor in Elementary Education - ( 260000QS ) TU Search Number : COE-4022 Assistant Professor in Elementary Education Department of Elementary Education College of Education COE-4022 Towson University: Towson University (TU) is one of the nation\u2019s top 100 public universities. Located north of Baltimore, TU currently enrolls over 19,000 students and is the second-largest university in the prestigious University System of Maryland. Towson University fosters a climate that is grounded in respect to cultivate the intellectual and personal growth of the entire university community. Position: The College of Education invites applications for a tenure-track, 9-month Assistant Professor position in the Department of Elementary Education with three years PreK-12 grade teaching experience in public schools. Faculty with expertise in elementary education curriculum and instruction with demonstrated knowledge and experience in reading instruction and assessment, writing instruction, and supporting multilingual learners are encouraged to apply. Preferred begin date is August 2027. Qualifications: Applicants should have a doctoral degree in Curriculum and Instruction or an education-related field. ABD applications will be considered, but the appointment will be at the instructor rank, and all degree requirements must be completed by August 1, 2027. Candidates should have a strong commitment to teaching and working with teacher candidates and novice teachers; e xpertise in elementary education literacy curriculum, instruction, and assessment; demonstrated knowledge and experience supporting multilingual learners and/or urban schools; a promise high-quality research; the ability to work in a collaborative manner with colleagues and school-based partners, and commitment to working across programs, disciplines, and cultures to strengthen the field. Responsibilities: Primary responsibilities include: (1) Teaching and Supervising: Research-active instructors teach/supervise 6 course units (equivalent to 18 credits) over a 9-month academic year in our student-focused programs, providing high-quality instruction at the undergraduate and graduate levels in a variety of literacy courses, (2) Scholarship: Development/continuation of a focused area of research that includes peer-reviewed publications, professional presentations, grant funding, and involvement in scholarly projects with students; and (3) Service: Active service participation at the department, college, university, community, and professional levels. The Department: The Department of Elementary Education currently has 28 full time-time faculty members and offers four programs. The programs include: one undergraduate elementary education program and three graduate programs (M.Ed. in Reading Education, M.Ed. in Elementary Education, and M.A.T. in Elementary Education). The Department of Elementary Education also offers a minor in Linguistic Diversity and a Teaching Multilingual Learners Graduate Certificate. College of Education is the longest-standing, largest and preeminent producer of teachers in Maryland and nationally recognized as a leader in educator preparation. Application Process :\u00a0Review of applications begins immediately and continues until the positions are filled. Interested applicants should submit a (1) letter of application that addresses the posting details and qualifications. Applications should also include: (2) curriculum vitae, (3) research statement that addresses current and future research agenda, (4) three letters of recommendation, (5) contact information (name, address, email, phone number) for three professional references (may be those who wrote letters of recommendation), and (6) graduate transcripts (official or unofficial). Application materials should be submitted electronically via the application link. Questions should be directed to eled@towson.edu Towson University. Please click here to apply. Please note that the search number for which you are applying is COE-4022. Please be sure to visit the Applicant Data Form to complete a voluntary on-line form. All data collected are for internal, state, and/or federal reporting and will not be used for other purposes. Salary and Benefits: Targeted salary range is $70,000-$73,000, commensurate with experience. Benefits: TU offers a comprehensive benefits package that includes excellent health, life and retirement plans; and tuition remission. To learn more about our benefits, click here for regular faculty/regular lecturer or here for contingent lecturer. TU also offers a variety of great perks and discounts, which can be found here. Background Check: A Criminal Background Investigation is required for the hired candidate and the results may impact employment. COVID-19 Statement: The safety of our students, faculty, staff, and neighbors has been our top priority and the focus of every one of our decisions since the earliest days of the COVID-19 pandemic. Therefore, the University System of Maryland (USM) has strongly encouraged full COVID vaccination and up-to-date booster shots (when eligible) for all faculty, staff, and students at all schools in the USM as both a reasonable and necessary means of protecting our health and safety. Organization : Academic Affairs Division Primary Location : Main Campus Job Posting : Oct 2, 2026 Towson University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. If you need a reasonable accommodation for any part of the employment process, please send an email to: adarequest@towson.edu Towson University is a smoke-free campus. \u00a92016 | 8000 York Road | Towson, MD 21252 | 410-704-2000"}, "https://towson.taleo.net/careersection/fac_ex/jobdetail.ftl?job=260000CU": {"title": "Assistant Teaching Professor", "description": "Job Description - Assistant Teaching Professor (260000CU) Go to the main content section. Welcome.  You are not signed in.  NOTE: If you experience any issues with this page, please contact the Towson University Office of Human Resources at 410-704-2162. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Assistant Teaching Professor (260000CU) Job Description Assistant Teaching Professor - ( 260000CU ) TU Search Number : COE-3922L Assistant Teaching Professor Department of Learning Technologies, Design & School Library Media (LTDM) College of Education COE-3922L Towson University: Towson University (TU) is one of the nation\u2019s top 100 public universities. Located north of Baltimore, TU currently enrolls over 19,000 students and is the second-largest university in the prestigious University System of Maryland. Towson University fosters a climate that is grounded in respect to cultivate the intellectual and personal growth of the entire university community. Position: The College of Education, Department of Learning Technologies, Design & School Library Media (LTDM) at Towson University invites applications for a non-tenure, 9-month Assistant Teaching Professor position in the Learning Design/Instructional Technology programs. Spring 2027 preferred start date. The LTDM Department offers Ph.D., M.S., and certificate programs in instructional design and development, educational technology, and school library media. It also offers undergraduate courses in \u201cintegrating technology in teaching and learning,\u201d \u201cartificial intelligence for education,\u201d and \u201ccybersecurity for educators\u201d for prospective teachers and other interested undergraduates, as well as several sections of general education freshman research seminars. Qualifications: The teaching-focused faculty position emphasizes computing, artificial intelligence (AI), data science, and advanced technology integration , grounded in learning design and learning sciences . The successful candidate will contribute to undergraduate and/or graduate programs by designing and teaching innovative, student-centered courses that engage learners through problem- and project-based learning, promote inclusive excellence, and prepare students to apply computational and data-driven approaches to real-world challenges. This role is ideal for educators who bridge technical expertise with evidence-based teaching practices and who are passionate about broadening participation in computing and learning technologies. Successful candidates will have: \u00b7 earned a master\u2019s or Ph.D. in Computer Science, Data Science, Artificial Intelligence, Learning Sciences, Cognitive Psychology, Educational Technology, or a closely related field; \u00b7 demonstrated commitment to culturally responsive teaching and mentoring diverse student populations; \u00b7 show evidence of teaching experience or strong potential for excellence in teaching at the undergraduate and/or graduate level; \u00b7 demonstrated expertise in at least one of the following areas: Artificial intelligence or machine learning; Data science or data analytics; Computing/Computer Science; Cognitive Psychology/Learning Sciences; \u00b7 show familiarity with ethical, societal, and policy issues related to AI and data science; \u00b7 evidence of skill in designing authentic, real-world learning experiences; \u00b7 demonstrated commitment to continuous improvement through reflective and evidence-based teaching; \u00b7 show strong communication and collaboration skills; and \u00b7 evidence of pedagogical scholarship, curriculum development, or teaching\u2011related grants. Responsibilities: Design and teach courses in areas such as: Artificial intelligence and machine learning; Data science and data literacy; Computing foundations (e.g., programming, algorithms, systems); integrating advanced learning technology in teaching and learning; ethics and societal impacts of AI and computing Develop interdisciplinary, project-based learning experiences grounded in authentic problems. Continuously assess and improve courses using student feedback, learning data, and reflective practice. \u00b7 Develop scholarship and curriculum development through engagement in professional development and reflective, evidence-based teaching. Application Process: Review of applications begins immediately and continues until the position is filled. Submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, candidate\u2019s reflections, and descriptions of your experience and background that match the position qualification, graduate transcripts, and three reference letters to the link below . Click here to apply. Please note that the search number for which you are applying is COE-3922L. Please be sure to visit the Applicant Data Form to complete a voluntary online form. All data collected is for internal, state, and/or federal reporting and will not be used for other purposes. Salary and Benefits: Targeted salary range: $50,000 - $55,000, commensurate with experience. Benefits: TU offers a comprehensive benefits package that includes excellent health, life and retirement plans; and tuition remission. To learn more about our benefits, click here for regular faculty/teaching professor or here for contingent teaching professor. TU also offers a variety of great perks and discounts, which can be found here . Background Check: A Criminal Background Investigation is required for the hired candidate, and the results may impact employment. COVID-19 Statement: The safety of our students, faculty, staff, and neighbors has been our top priority and the focus of every decision we have made since the earliest days of the COVID-19 pandemic. Therefore, the University System of Maryland (USM) has strongly encouraged full COVID vaccination and up-to-date booster shots (when eligible) for all faculty, staff, and students at all USM schools, as both a reasonable and necessary means of protecting our health and safety. Organization : Academic Affairs Division Primary Location : Main Campus Job Posting : May 21, 2026 Towson University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. If you need a reasonable accommodation for any part of the employment process, please send an email to: adarequest@towson.edu Towson University is a smoke-free campus. \u00a92016 | 8000 York Road | Towson, MD 21252 | 410-704-2000"}, "https://towson.taleo.net/careersection/fac_ex/jobdetail.ftl?job=260000IE": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Printmaking", "description": "Job Description - Assistant Professor of Printmaking (260000IE) Go to the main content section. Welcome.  You are not signed in.  NOTE: If you experience any issues with this page, please contact the Towson University Office of Human Resources at 410-704-2162. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Assistant Professor of Printmaking (260000IE) Job Description Assistant Professor of Printmaking - ( 260000IE ) TU Search Number : COFAC-4003 Assistant Professor of Printmaking Department of Art + Design, Art History, Art Education College of Fine Arts and Communication COFAC-4003 Towson University Towson University is one of the nation\u2019s top 100 public universities. Located north of Baltimore, TU currently enrolls over 19,000 students and is the second-largest university in the prestigious University System of Maryland. Towson University fosters a climate that is grounded in respect to cultivate the intellectual and personal growth of the entire university community. Position The College of Fine Arts and Communication invites applications for a tenure-track, 9-month Assistant Professor of Printmaking position in the Department of Art + Design, Art History, Art Education. Preferred start date: August 2027. The department seeks an artist-educator with strong creative practice, a demonstrated commitment to undergraduate teaching, and the ability to lead and support a dynamic printmaking area. The successful candidate will teach printmaking courses at multiple levels, oversee the printmaking facility, contribute to the development of the printmaking curriculum, maintain an active creative/research agenda, and participate in departmental, college, university, and professional service. We welcome applicants whose work demonstrates strong technical, conceptual, and historical engagement with printmaking, including traditional, contemporary, expanded, and/or interdisciplinary approaches. Qualifications Required Qualifications \u00b7 MFA or terminal degree in Printmaking, Studio Art, or a closely related field by the start date. \u00b7 Evidence of an active creative/research practice in printmaking \u00b7 Demonstrated ability to teach undergraduate printmaking courses. \u00b7 Strong knowledge of printmaking techniques, histories, theories, and contemporary practices. \u00b7 Commitment to inclusive, student-centered teaching and mentorship. \u00b7 Evidence of professional engagement through exhibitions, publications, residencies, grants, commissions, collaborations, curatorial projects, community-based projects \u00b7 Ability to support safe, responsible, and effective use of printmaking facilities, equipment, tools, and materials. Including but not limited to knowledge of safe shop practices, equipment maintenance, chemical safety, ventilation needs, and sustainable/non-toxic printmaking processes. Preferred Qualifications \u00b7 College-level teaching experience beyond graduate assistantships. \u00b7 Experience teaching printmaking at multiple levels, including introductory, intermediate, and advanced courses. \u00b7 Experience managing or helping maintain a printmaking studio, shop, lab, or shared studio environment. \u00b7 Ability to teach across a range of printmaking processes, including both traditional and contemporary/digital approaches. \u00b7 Ability to contribute to curriculum development and help build a forward-looking printmaking area within a broad art and design department. Responsibilities Responsibilities include: \u00b7 Teaching undergraduate and graduate printmaking students at multiple levels. Teaching may include foundational, intermediate, and advanced printmaking courses, as well as courses that serve the broader studio art curriculum depending on departmental needs and the candidate\u2019s expertise. Current printmaking offerings include courses in silkscreen, intaglio, lithography, relief, letterpress, book arts, and painterly and digital approaches. \u00b7 Acting as area coordinator for printmaking, which serves students in the combined Painting, Drawing, Printmaking concentration as well as students in other studio areas, Art Education and Art History. The area coordinator manages and maintains the printmaking facility, including equipment, supplies, and safe studio procedures, develops and oversees the printmaking curriculum, and contributes to building a vibrant departmental community. \u00b7 Maintaining an active creative/research agenda appropriate to a tenure-track faculty appointment. \u00b7 Participating in advising, assessment, recruitment, committee work, and other forms of departmental, college, university, and professional service. The standard workload for tenure-track faculty in the Department of Art + Design, Art History, Art Education is to teach 6, three-credit classes per academic year at undergraduate and graduate levels as assigned. The Department Facilities consist of well-equipped studios and labs for metals, jewelry, ceramics, sculpture, illustration, painting, drawing, printmaking, photography, digital and graphic arts. Other departmental resources include a comprehensive digital fabrication and rapid technologies lab, and two galleries. Application Process Review of applications begins December 1st, 2026 and continues until the position is filled. Applicants must submit all materials through Taleo. Applicants cannot apply by email. Complete applications should include: \u00b7 Cover letter addressing qualifications, teaching experience, creative/research practice, and interest in the position. \u00b7 Curriculum vitae. \u00b7 Artist statement. \u00b7 Teaching philosophy addressing inclusive teaching, mentorship, and student success. \u00b7 Portfolio of professional creative work: 20 examples, submitted as a single PDF or dedicated website link. \u00b7 Examples of student work, if available: 20 examples maximum, submitted as a single PDF or dedicated website link. \u00b7 Sample syllabi or course materials. \u00b7 Unofficial graduate transcript. \u00b7 Names and contact information for three professional references. Click here to apply. Please note that the search number for which you are applying is COFAC-4003. Please be sure to visit the Applicant Data Form to complete a voluntary online form. All data collected are for internal, state, and/or federal reporting and will not be used for other purposes. Salary and Benefits Targeted salary range: $70,000 Benefits: TU offers a comprehensive benefits package that includes excellent health, life and retirement plans; and tuition remission. To learn more about our benefits, click here for regular faculty/regular lecturer or here for contingent lecturer. TU also offers a variety of great perks and discounts, which can be found here. Background Check: A Criminal Background Investigation is required for the hired candidate and the results may impact employment. COVID-19 Statement: The safety of our students, faculty, staff, and neighbors has been our top priority and the focus of every one of our decisions since the earliest days of the COVID-19 pandemic. Therefore, the University System of Maryland (USM) has strongly encouraged full COVID vaccination and up- to-date booster shots (when eligible) for all faculty, staff, and students at all schools in the USM as both a reasonable and necessary means of protecting our health and safety. Organization : Academic Affairs Division Primary Location : Main Campus Job Posting : Jul 7, 2026 Towson University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. If you need a reasonable accommodation for any part of the employment process, please send an email to: adarequest@towson.edu Towson University is a smoke-free campus. \u00a92016 | 8000 York Road | Towson, MD 21252 | 410-704-2000"}, "https://towson.taleo.net/careersection/fac_ex/jobdetail.ftl?job=260000I8": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Communication", "description": "Job Description - Assistant Professor of Communication (260000I8) Go to the main content section. Welcome.  You are not signed in.  NOTE: If you experience any issues with this page, please contact the Towson University Office of Human Resources at 410-704-2162. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Assistant Professor of Communication (260000I8) Job Description Assistant Professor of Communication - ( 260000I8 ) TU Search Number : COFAC-4004 Assistant Professor Department of Communication Studies College of Fine Arts and Communication COFAC-4004 Towson University: Towson University (TU) is one of the nation\u2019s top 100 public universities. Located north of Baltimore, TU currently enrolls over 19,000 students and is the second-largest university in the prestigious University System of Maryland. Towson University fosters a climate that is grounded in respect to cultivate the intellectual and personal growth of the entire university community. Position: The College of Fine Arts & Communication invites applications for a tenure-track, 9-month Assistant Professor position in the Department of Communication Studies. Preferred start date August, 2027. Qualifications: The successful candidate will hold or anticipate a Ph.D. in Communication or a related field at the time of appointment (August 1, 2027). Candidates will demonstrate success or potential as a classroom teacher and researcher across multiple qualitative research methods such as cutting-edge critical, performance, rhetoric, and arts-based methods. Candidates must have a commitment to teaching and mentoring/advising undergraduate and graduate students. Candidates should be able to demonstrate a commitment to interdisciplinary scholarship with a potential for partnering across the department, university, and community and for securing internal and external funding. Candidates must have a broad commitment to critical communication pedagogy and be able to teach qualitative research courses especially the following undergraduate core courses: Introduction to Communication Studies, Critical Writing and Research, and Critical Research Methods. At the graduate level, candidates should be able to teach Advanced Qualitative Research Methods and Advanced Communication Theory. We also seek a colleague whose scholarship, embodied work, and teaching align with but is not limited to critical/humanistic communication theories and methods to emerging trends in health communication, environmental communication, digital communication, organizational and leadership communication, intercultural communication, or interpersonal communication. Candidates whose work addresses interdisciplinary fields such as disability studies, races and ethnic studies, queer and trans studies, native and indigenous knowledge, and artificial intelligence policy will also be considered. Successful candidates may have the opportunity to teach elective classes and/or develop additional electives related to their area of research expertise. Responsibilities: For the first year, research-active faculty teach five or six classes over a 9-month academic year with undergraduate class sizes averaging 22 students per class and graduate class sizes averaging 15 students per class. Candidates may teach courses at the Towson University Northeast (TUNE) campus on a rotating basis, as needed. We encourage candidates whose research intersects with or extends department strengths in embodied communicative praxis to engage in social activism and advocacy. Scholarly research productivity and service, including mentoring and advising, to the department, college, and university is expected. The Department: The department ( www.towson.edu/comm ) offers an undergraduate major in Communication Studies and undergraduate minors in Communication Studies, Cultural Studies, and Professional Communication. At the graduate level, the department offers a Master of Arts in Communication and Advocacy. The department offers the majors and minors at our main campus and our Towson University Northeast (TUNE) campus and annually enrolls approximately 300 majors served by 14 full-time and 25 part-time faculty members.\u00a0Department faculty specialize in rhetoric, organizational communication, critical/cultural studies, performance studies, intercultural communication, and critical/qualitative research methods. Application Process: Review of applications will commence October 2, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. Applicants should submit: \u00b7 A letter of application addressing the candidate\u2019s unique profile in relation to this position\u00a0and the department. \u00b7 A current CV with the names of at least three references and contact information (letters of recommendation may be requested from candidates who continue to a later stage of the process). \u00b7 A teaching effectiveness portfolio that includes your teaching philosophy and potential or demonstrated evidence of teaching effectiveness which articulates your broad commitment to communication pedagogy \u00b7 A research statement that charts your scholarly expertise and agenda \u00b7 An unofficial copy of graduate transcripts Click here to apply. Please note that the search number for which you are applying is COFAC-4004. Please be sure to visit the Applicant Data Form to complete a voluntary on-line form. All data collected are for internal, state, and/or federal reporting and will not be used for other purposes. Salary and Benefits: Targeted salary range: $67,000 - $70,000. Benefits: TU offers a comprehensive benefits package that includes excellent health, life and retirement plans; and tuition remission. To learn more about our benefits, click here for regular faculty/regular lecturer or here for contingent lecturer. TU also offers a variety of great perks and discounts, which can be found here. Background Check: A Criminal Background Investigation is required for the hired candidate and the results may impact employment. COVID-19 Statement: The safety of our students, faculty, staff, and neighbors has been our top priority and the focus of every one of our decisions since the earliest days of the COVID-19 pandemic. Therefore, the University System of Maryland (USM) has strongly encouraged full COVID vaccination and up- to-date booster shots (when eligible) for all faculty, staff, and students at all schools in the USM as both a reasonable and necessary means of protecting our health and safety. Organization : Academic Affairs Division Primary Location : Main Campus Job Posting : Jul 6, 2026 Towson University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. If you need a reasonable accommodation for any part of the employment process, please send an email to: adarequest@towson.edu Towson University is a smoke-free campus. \u00a92016 | 8000 York Road | Towson, MD 21252 | 410-704-2000"}, "https://towson.taleo.net/careersection/fac_ex/jobdetail.ftl?job=260000I5": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Audio Production", "description": "Job Description - Assistant Professor of Audio Production (260000I5) Go to the main content section. Welcome.  You are not signed in.  NOTE: If you experience any issues with this page, please contact the Towson University Office of Human Resources at 410-704-2162. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Assistant Professor of Audio Production (260000I5) Job Description Assistant Professor of Audio Production - ( 260000I5 ) TU Search Number : COFAC-4000 Assistant Professor Film, Audio, Media Arts College of Fine Arts and Communication COFAC-4000 Towson University: Towson University (TU) is one of the nation\u2019s top 100 public universities. Located north of Baltimore, TU currently enrolls over 19,000 students and is the second-largest university in the prestigious University System of Maryland. Towson University fosters a climate that is grounded in respect to cultivate the intellectual and personal growth of the entire university community. Position: The College of Fine Arts and Communication invites applications for a tenure-track, 9-month Assistant Professor position in the Film, Audio, Media Arts Department. Preferred start date August 2027. Qualifications: Master of Fine Arts or doctorate degree in audio and media production, or a related field, received by June 2027. The Film, Audio, Media Arts Department seeks candidates with a vision for the future of audio production for media and audio content creation. Demonstrated expertise in digital audio workstation software is required; experience with Avid\u2019s Pro Tools preferred. Demonstrated expertise in one or more of the following is required: studio sound recording and mixing, sound design for visual media, podcasting and/or radio production. Experience with audio over internet protocol (AoIP) systems, particularly Audinate\u2019s Dante network, is preferred but not required. Demonstrated success in teaching, or demonstrated potential to teach audio production, audio studio, and/or audio broadcast courses at the undergraduate level is required. A demonstrated record of related scholarship/artistic research/professional activity is required. Applicants with additional specialties in multimedia production, live sound production, sound-based installation and media art, or sound theory and aesthetics are encouraged to apply. Responsibilities: Research-active faculty teach 6 classes over a 9-month academic year (3 per semester) with undergraduate class size averaging 20 students per class. Undergraduate teaching is expected to include foundational audio production courses for both audio and film-focused students as well as intermediate and advanced courses focusing on specific aspects of audio production utilizing our recording and mixing studios. There may be opportunities to develop new courses in the candidate\u2019s area of expertise and interest. Undergraduate advising is part of the position\u2019s teaching responsibilities. Scholarly/artistic research productivity and service to the department, college, and university are expected. Service responsibilities will include leadership of student organizations that produce media content. The Department: The Film, Audio, Media Arts Department is the largest and most comprehensive media and film department in Maryland. FAMA provides a rigorous media arts education in which students learn to tell their own stories, hone their craft, and make meaningful media. FAMA students choose from one of three concentrations: Film/Video/Digital Media, Audio, and Film and Media Studies. Within these concentrations, our 400+ FAMA majors and minors develop skills in writing, media history and criticism, and professional media production for narrative, documentary, experimental, and new media forms. Towson University\u2019s Film, Audio, Media Arts Department is made up of 15 full-time and over 20 part-time faculty. In academic year 2027-2028, the Film, Audio, Media Arts Department will be moving into the newly renovated and reconstructed Smith Hall that will include state-of-the-art studios, labs, production facilities, classrooms, and a cinema theatre. Application Process: Review of applications begins immediately and continues until the position is filled. For best consideration, applications should be submitted by November 1, 2026. Submissions require the following: \u00b7 cover letter describing your job qualifications and professional experience, and including a statement on candidate\u2019s artistic/scholarly research \u00b7 curriculum vitae \u00b7 a list of three references (including current contact information). Candidates who advance to the on-campus interview stage of the process will be required to submit three letters of recommendation (sent under separate covers) \u00b7 an unofficial copy of graduate transcripts (official transcripts are required prior to hire) \u00b7 a teaching effectiveness portfolio that includes your teaching philosophy and materials such as student and peer evaluations that show demonstrated or potential evidence of teaching effectiveness (ex. student or peer evaluations of college courses taught, assessments or feedback on graduate teaching assistantships, assessments of workshops or mentorships you have led, etc.) \u00b7 a portfolio/reel (submitted as a PDF with descriptions and URLs of media projects) demonstrating your creative/scholarly work Click here to apply. Please note that the search number for which you are applying is COFAC-4000. Please be sure to visit the Applicant Data Form to complete a voluntary on-line form. All data collected are for internal, state, and/or federal reporting and will not be used for other purposes. Salary and Benefits: Targeted salary range: $68,000 - $70,000 commensurate with experience. Benefits: TU offers a comprehensive benefits package that includes excellent health, life and retirement plans; and tuition remission. To learn more about our benefits, click here for regular faculty/regular lecturer or here for contingent lecturer. TU also offers a variety of great perks and discounts, which can be found here. Background Check: A Criminal Background Investigation is required for the hired candidate and the results may impact employment. COVID-19 Statement: The safety of our students, faculty, staff, and neighbors has been our top priority and the focus of every one of our decisions since the earliest days of the COVID-19 pandemic. Therefore, the University System of Maryland (USM) has strongly encouraged full COVID vaccination and up- to-date booster shots (when eligible) for all faculty, staff, and students at all schools in the USM as both a reasonable and necessary means of protecting our health and safety. Organization : Academic Affairs Division Primary Location : Main Campus Job Posting : Jul 2, 2026 Towson University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. If you need a reasonable accommodation for any part of the employment process, please send an email to: adarequest@towson.edu Towson University is a smoke-free campus. \u00a92016 | 8000 York Road | Towson, MD 21252 | 410-704-2000"}, "https://towson.taleo.net/careersection/fac_ex/jobdetail.ftl?job=260000IA": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Advertising", "description": "Job Description - Assistant Professor of Advertising (260000IA) Go to the main content section. Welcome.  You are not signed in.  NOTE: If you experience any issues with this page, please contact the Towson University Office of Human Resources at 410-704-2162. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Assistant Professor of Advertising (260000IA) Job Description Assistant Professor of Advertising - ( 260000IA ) TU Search Number : COFAC-4005 Assistant Professor, Advertising Department of Mass Communication College of Fine Arts and Communication COFAC-4005 Towson University: Towson University (TU) is one of the nation\u2019s top 100 public universities. Located north of Baltimore, TU currently enrolls over 19,000 students and is the second-largest university in the prestigious University System of Maryland. Towson University fosters a climate that is grounded in respect to cultivate the intellectual and personal growth of the entire university community. Position: The College of Fine Arts and Communication invites applications for a tenure-track, nine-month Assistant Professor in Advertising position in the Department of Mass Communication. Preferred start date August 2027. Qualifications: Ph.D. in strategic communication, mass communication, advertising, or related fields. ABD applicants will be considered, but appointment will be at the Instructor rank, and all doctorate degree requirements must be completed by February 1, 2028. Demonstrated success or potential to teach advertising courses at undergraduate and graduate levels. Demonstrated potential to develop a strong body of scholarship. Responsibilities: Research-active faculty teach six classes over a nine-month academic year with undergraduate classes averaging 20 students and graduate classes averaging about 15 students. Undergraduate teaching may include Advertising Copywriting, Advertising Media Planning, Principles of Advertising, Advertising Campaigns, or other advertising courses. Graduate teaching may include Qualitative/Quantitative Research Methods in Communication, Social Media Content Strategies, Social Media Analytics, Communication Theory, Consumer Psychology, or others in the candidate\u2019s areas of scholarship and expertise. Contribute to the department's strategic priorities by integrating emerging technologies such as artificial intelligence (AI) into teaching and research relevant to advertising and strategic communication. May also develop or teach courses that intersect with advertising and sports communication. Expected to advise undergraduate students and supervise graduate student theses or professional projects. Scholarly research productivity and service to the department, college, and university are expected. The Department: The department ( https://www.towson.edu/cofac/departments/mass-communication/ ) offers an undergraduate major in Mass Communication with tracks in Advertising, Strategic Public Relations, and Digital and Broadcast Journalism. At the graduate level, the department offers a Master of Science in Communication Management. The department annually enrolls over 400 majors served by 21 full-time faculty and over 20 part-time faculty, and will be housed in the new, state-of-the-art Smith Hall in 2027. Application Process: Review of applications begins on September 28, 2026, and continues until the position is filled. Please direct inquiries to the chair of the search committee, Dr. Soo Rhee, erhee@towson.edu . For initial applications, submit: Cover letter / letter of application Curriculum vitae with a list of three references An unofficial copy of graduate transcripts A teaching effectiveness portfolio that includes a teaching philosophy, potential or demonstrated evidence of teaching effectiveness Candidates who advance to the next stage of the process will be required to submit: A research statement Three letters of recommendation (sent under separate covers) Official transcripts are required prior to hire. Click here to apply. Please note that the search number for which you are applying is COFAC - 4005 . Please be sure to visit the Applicant Data Form to complete a voluntary on-line form. All data collected are for internal, state, and/or federal reporting and will not be used for other purposes. Salary and Benefits: Targeted salary range: $67,000 - $70,000. Benefits: TU offers a comprehensive benefits package that includes excellent health, life and retirement plans; and tuition remission. To learn more about our benefits, click here for regular faculty/regular lecturer or here for contingent lecturer. TU also offers a variety of great perks and discounts, which can be found here . Background Check: A Criminal Background Investigation is required for the hired candidate and the results may impact employment. COVID-19 Statement: The safety of our students, faculty, staff, and neighbors has been our top priority and the focus of every one of our decisions since the earliest days of the COVID-19 pandemic. Therefore, the University System of Maryland (USM) has strongly encouraged full COVID vaccination and up- to-date booster shots (when eligible) for all faculty, staff, and students at all schools in the USM as both a reasonable and necessary means of protecting our health and safety. Organization : Academic Affairs Division Primary Location : Main Campus Job Posting : Jul 7, 2026 Towson University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. If you need a reasonable accommodation for any part of the employment process, please send an email to: adarequest@towson.edu Towson University is a smoke-free campus. \u00a92016 | 8000 York Road | Towson, MD 21252 | 410-704-2000"}, "https://towson.taleo.net/careersection/fac_ex/jobdetail.ftl?job=260000IH": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Public Relations", "description": "Job Description - Assistant Professor of Public Relations (260000IH) Go to the main content section. Welcome.  You are not signed in.  NOTE: If you experience any issues with this page, please contact the Towson University Office of Human Resources at 410-704-2162. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Assistant Professor of Public Relations (260000IH) Job Description Assistant Professor of Public Relations - ( 260000IH ) TU Search Number : COFAC-4006 Assistant Professor, Public Relations Department of Mass Communication College of Fine Arts and Communication COFAC-4006 Towson University Towson University (TU) is one of the nation\u2019s top 100 public universities. Located north of Baltimore, TU currently enrolls more than 19,000 students and is the second-largest university in the prestigious University System of Maryland. Towson University fosters a climate grounded in respect that cultivates the intellectual and personal growth of the entire university community. Position The College of Fine Arts and Communication invites applications for a tenure-track, nine-month Assistant Professor in Public Relations in the Department of Mass Communication. Preferred start date: August 2027. Qualifications Ph.D. in Public Relations, Strategic Communication, Mass Communication, or a related field. ABD applicants will be considered, but appointment will be at the Instructor rank, and all doctorate degree requirements must be completed by February 1, 2028. Demonstrated success or potential to teach public relations courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels. Demonstrated potential to develop a strong body of scholarship. Applicants whose teaching draws from professional experience in strategic public relations or related fields are encouraged to apply. Responsibilities Research-active faculty teach six classes over a nine-month academic year with undergraduate classes averaging 20 students and graduate classes averaging approximately 15 students. Undergraduate teaching may include Public Relations Writing, Corporate Communication Management, Strategic Public Relations Campaigns, Principles of Strategic Public Relations, Social Media and Strategic Communication, and other public relations courses. Graduate teaching may include Practice of Public Relations and Organizational Communication, Social Media Content Strategies, Qualitative/Quantitative Research Methods in Communication, Social Media Analytics, Crisis Communication, Media Relations, or other courses aligned with the applicant\u2019s scholarship and expertise. Applicants whose innovative research expands the department\u2019s scholarly reach and opens new avenues for curriculum development in public relations, sports communication, and related fields are welcome. Applications from scholars whose work explores the intersection of artificial intelligence, sports sponsorships, sustainability, and strategic communication, including implications for society, health, technologies, consumer outcomes, and media effects, are encouraged. The Department The Department of Mass Communication ( https://www.towson.edu/cofac/departments/mass-communication/ ) offers an undergraduate major in Mass Communication with tracks in Advertising, Strategic Public Relations, and Digital and Broadcast Journalism. At the graduate level, the department offers a Master of Science in Communication Management. The department annually enrolls more than 400 majors served by 21 full-time faculty and over 20 part-time faculty and will be housed in the new state-of-the-art Smith Hall in 2027. Application Process Review of applications begins on September 14, 2026 , and continues until the position is filled. Please direct inquiries to the chair of the search committee, Dr. Hyang-Sook Kim, at hkim@towson.edu . For initial applications, submit: A cover letter summarizing qualifications for the position Curriculum vitae An unofficial copy of graduate transcripts The names and contact information of three references Candidates who advance to the next stage of the process will be required to submit: A teaching effectiveness portfolio that includes a teaching philosophy, as well as potential or demonstrated evidence of teaching effectiveness supporting TU and departmental goals A research statement Three letters of recommendation (submitted separately) Official transcripts prior to hire Click here to apply. Please note that the search number for this position is COFAC-4006 . Please be sure to visit the Applicant Data Form to complete a voluntary online form. All data collected are used only for internal, state, and/or federal reporting purposes and will not be used for any other purpose. Salary and Benefits Targeted salary range: $67,000\u2013$70,000. TU offers a comprehensive benefits package that includes excellent health, life, and retirement plans as well as tuition remission. Learn more about faculty benefits here . TU also offers a variety of employee perks and discounts, which can be found here . Background Check A Criminal Background Investigation is required for the selected candidate, and the results may impact employment. COVID-19 Statement The safety of our students, faculty, staff, and neighbors has been our top priority and the focus of our decisions since the earliest days of the COVID-19 pandemic. Therefore, the University System of Maryland has strongly encouraged full COVID vaccination and up-to-date booster shots (when eligible) for faculty, staff, and students as a reasonable and necessary means of protecting community health and safety. Organization : Academic Affairs Division Primary Location : Main Campus Job Posting : Jul 9, 2026 Towson University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. If you need a reasonable accommodation for any part of the employment process, please send an email to: adarequest@towson.edu Towson University is a smoke-free campus. \u00a92016 | 8000 York Road | Towson, MD 21252 | 410-704-2000"}, "https://towson.taleo.net/careersection/fac_ex/jobdetail.ftl?job=260000OO": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Elementary and Early Childhood Vocal-General Music Education", "description": "Job Description - Assistant Professor of Elementary and Early Childhood Vocal-General Music Education (260000OO) Go to the main content section. Welcome.  You are not signed in.  NOTE: If you experience any issues with this page, please contact the Towson University Office of Human Resources at 410-704-2162. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Assistant Professor of Elementary and Early Childhood Vocal-General Music Education (260000OO) Job Description Assistant Professor of Elementary and Early Childhood Vocal-General Music Education - ( 260000OO ) TU Search Number : COFAC 4020 Assistant Professor of Elementary and Early Childhood Vocal-General Music Education Department of Music College of Fine Arts and Communication COFAC-4020 Towson University: Towson University (TU) is one of the nation\u2019s top 100 public universities. Located north of Baltimore, TU currently enrolls over 19,000 students and is the second-largest university in the prestigious University System of Maryland. Towson University fosters a climate that is grounded in respect to cultivate the intellectual and personal growth of the entire university community. Position: The College of Fine Arts and Communication invites applications for a tenure-track, 9-month Assistant Professor of Elementary and Early Childhood Vocal General Music Education position in the Department of Music. Preferred start date is August 2027. This position focuses on elementary/early childhood vocal-general music education, with additional music education courses assigned according to faculty expertise and departmental needs. We welcome applicants with a broad range of experience in the following areas: vocal-general music at the elementary/early childhood level, music education pedagogies, foundations of music education, internship (student teaching) supervision, and related areas of vocal-general music education. Applicants should demonstrate a commitment to inclusive practices in music education across urban, suburban, and rural communities. We seek an innovative, student-centered teacher-scholar who demonstrates excellence in teaching, scholarly engagement in music education, and service. Additional compensated summer teaching may be available. Qualifications: Minimum Required Qualifications include: \u00b7 Earned doctorate in music education required; ABD (all-but-dissertation) applicants will be considered, but appointment prior to completing the doctorate will be at the Instructor rank, and all doctoral degree requirements must be completed by August 1, 2027. \u00b7 A minimum of three years of full-time public/private school teaching experience is required. \u00b7 Evidence of a strong background in vocal-general music education at the elementary and/or early childhood levels. \u00b7 Training in common general music pedagogies, which may include Kod\u00e1ly, Orff-Schulwerk, Dalcroze Eurhythmics, Music Learning Theory, World Music Drumming, and/or Modern Band/Popular Music. Desired Qualifications include: \u00b7 Experience teaching in higher education in one or more of the following areas: elementary or early childhood vocal-general music methods, foundations of music education, music for elementary education majors, research and assessment, integrating literacy in the content area, introduction to music in special education, student intern supervision, and student intern seminar. \u00b7 Ability to incorporate ukulele instruction and pedagogy into courses as appropriate \u00b7 Specialization (certification/levels) in one or more general music education pedagogies \u00b7 Ability to infuse modern band/pop music pedagogy into music education coursework \u00b7 Ability to model and incorporate instruction on working with multilingual learners and students with special needs in music education coursework \u00b7 Commitment to student-centered education that meets the needs of variable learners \u00b7 Desire to collaborate and work in team situations \u00b7 Experience in curriculum development and/or program assessment \u00b7 Proficient use and modeling of technology/digital tools in face-to-face and/or online instruction \u00b7 Evidence of emerging scholarship/creative activity in music education Responsibilities: This position includes the following responsibilities: \u00b7 Teach and co-teach courses in the undergraduate and graduate music education degree programs, which could include, but are not limited to, research and assessment methods, music in special education, elementary and early childhood vocal-general methods/pedagogy), foundation courses in music education, integrating literacy in the content area, student intern supervision, graduate courses in music education, mentorship for graduate music education capstone projects and theses, and other courses based on applicant skills and department needs. \u00b7 Work collegially with faculty in the various aspects of the music education program. \u00b7 Engage in curriculum development and assist with program assessment, as needed. \u00b7 Recruit students and develop collaborative relationships with the local, regional, and national music education community through school visits, conference presentations, and invited teacher professional development sessions. \u00b7 Engage in a trajectory of significant scholarship/creative activity and service commensurate with the expectations for promotion and tenure at Towson University. \u00b7 Participate actively in assigned service duties with the department, college, university, and community/profession. The Department: The Department of Music (http://www.towson.edu/music) is committed to fostering a learning community that reflects the diversity of the surrounding region and state. The Department enrolls a diverse student population of approximately 265 students served by 80 full- and part-time faculty. This comprehensive music program offers a variety of concentrations across bachelor's, master's, and applied graduate certificate programs. Towson University and the Department of Music are accredited by NASM, MSDE, and CAEP. The Department has a long history of philanthropic support for the educational needs of its students. Our alumni are respected educators in PreK-12 schools and university settings, performers at the national and international levels, commercial musicians and jazz artists, entrepreneurs, and arts administrators. Application Process: Review of applications begins immediately and continues until the position is filled. Priority will be given to complete digital applications received by October 11, 2026. All materials must be submitted online through Taleo, the university's application portal. A complete application includes: [1] a letter of application addressing the candidate's qualifications for the position; [2] a curriculum vitae; [3] a reference page with names and contact information for at least three references; [4] a statement of teaching philosophy that includes discussion of inclusive teaching practices [5] a research statement outlining current and future scholarly interests; [6] unofficial transcripts from all institutions of higher education attended (official transcripts will be required at time of hire); and [7] a recent sample teaching video (up to 15 minutes of up to two clips) demonstrating vocal- general classroom instruction (university level preferred), accessible via a weblink to a streaming video platform. Additional materials may be requested later. Please address questions to: Dr. Kate Evans, Music Education Search Chair Department of Music Towson University 8000 York Road Towson, MD 21252 Phone: 410-704-2257 Email: muedsearch@towson.edu Click here to apply. Please note that the search number for which you are applying is COFAC-4020. Please be sure to visit the Applicant Data Form to complete a voluntary on-line form. All data collected are for internal, state, and/or federal reporting and will not be used for other purposes. Salary and Benefits: Targeted salary range: $67,000 - $70,000 commensurate with experience. Benefits: TU offers a comprehensive benefits package that includes excellent health, life and retirement plans; and tuition remission. To learn more about our benefits, click here for regular faculty/regular lecturer or here for contingent lecturer. TU also offers a variety of great perks and discounts, which can be found here. Background Check: A Criminal Background Investigation is required for the hired candidate and the results may impact employment. COVID-19 Statement: The safety of our students, faculty, staff, and neighbors has been our top priority and the focus of every one of our decisions since the earliest days of the COVID-19 pandemic. Therefore, the University System of Maryland (USM) has strongly encouraged full COVID vaccination and up-to-date booster shots (when eligible) for all faculty, staff, and students at all schools in the USM as both a reasonable and necessary means of protecting our health and safety. Organization : Academic Affairs Division Primary Location : Main Campus Job Posting : Sep 11, 2026 Towson University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. If you need a reasonable accommodation for any part of the employment process, please send an email to: adarequest@towson.edu Towson University is a smoke-free campus. \u00a92016 | 8000 York Road | Towson, MD 21252 | 410-704-2000"}, "https://towson.taleo.net/careersection/fac_ex/jobdetail.ftl?job=260000PV": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Composition", "description": "Job Description - Assistant Professor of Composition (260000PV) Go to the main content section. Welcome.  You are not signed in.  NOTE: If you experience any issues with this page, please contact the Towson University Office of Human Resources at 410-704-2162. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Assistant Professor of Composition (260000PV) Job Description Assistant Professor of Composition - ( 260000PV ) TU Search Number : COFAC 4024 Assistant Professor of Composition Department of Music College of Fine Arts and Communication COFAC-4024 Towson University: Towson University (TU) is one of the nation\u2019s top 100 public universities. Located north of Baltimore, TU currently enrolls over 19,000 students and is the second-largest university in the prestigious University System of Maryland. Towson University fosters a climate that is grounded in respect to cultivate the intellectual and personal growth of the entire university community. Position: The College of Fine Arts and Communication invites applications for a tenure-track, nine-month, full-time Assistant Professor of Composition in the Department of Music. The primary responsibility of this position is providing instruction in music composition to undergraduate and graduate students, through both private studio lessons and classroom teaching. Additional responsibilities include classroom teaching of music theory and musicianship and management of the Department of Music\u2019s Creative Technology Lab. The Department seeks an experienced, innovative, and student-centered educator who will demonstrate excellence in instruction, scholarship, and service. The p referred start date is August 2027. Qualifications: Applicants should hold a doctoral degree in composition. ABD candidates will be considered but must have completed a degree prior to appointment. Candidates must demonstrate excellence in teaching, a promising creative/scholarly agenda, and the capacity to serve the administrative needs of the Department of Music, the College of Fine Arts and Communication, and Towson University. Candidates with at least two years of university-level teaching experience are preferred. Responsibilities: Responsibilities of the position include 1) teaching composition lessons and mentoring student composers; 2) teaching music theory and musicianship classes; 3) maintaining an agenda of creative and scholarly work consistent with Towson University\u2019s reputation for excellence in interdisciplinary research; 4) managing the Department\u2019s Creative Technology Lab; 5) contributing to the development of an innovative music curriculum; 6) contributing to the growth of the composition program through active student recruitment; 7) demonstrating meaningful commitment to inclusive pedagogy and student engagement; 8) serving on department, college, and university committees; and 9) student advising. The Department: The Department of Music serves a community of over 200 music majors and graduate students, as well as offering courses and performance opportunities to students specializing in other fields. Towson students engage in a range of rigorous scholarly, creative, and collaborative work that reflects a broad base of musical interests. Our students have the valuable opportunity to work with a music faculty including internationally recognized composers, performers, scholars, and public intellectuals who prioritize student achievement, scholarly skills, creativity, and community. The Department regularly hosts guest artists for masterclasses and guest lectures and has a long history of philanthropic support to sponsor the educational needs of its students. TU alumni are nationally and internationally renowned composers and performers, educators in PreK-12 and university settings, technological innovators, entrepreneurs, and arts administrators. The Department offers three undergraduate degree programs for music majors: the Bachelor of Science in Music, the Bachelor of Music (classical performance, jazz/commercial performance, or composition), and the Bachelor of Science in Music Education. The Department also offers minors in general music, music industry, jazz/commercial performance, and music technology. Graduate degrees include the Master of Science in Music Education, the Master of Music, the Master of Music in Music Pedagogy, and the Graduate Certificate in Applied Music. Application Process: Review of applications begins immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Priority will be given to applications completed by November 15, 2026. All materials must be submitted online through the university's application portal. A complete application portfolio includes 1) a letter of application addressing the candidate\u2019s qualifications for the position; 2) a curriculum vitae; 3) a statement of teaching philosophy; 4) a statement describing current and future scholarly research; 5) a sample of creative work, preferably a web-accessible video or audio recording, with or without score; 6) three letters of recommendation; and 7) unofficial transcripts from all institutions of higher education attended (official transcripts will be required at time of hire). Confidential letters of recommendation should be sent to compositionsearch@towson.edu Note: Towson University is conducting a search for an Assistant Professor of Music Theory. Applicants wishing to be considered for both positions must submit a separate application for each. Enquiries should be addressed to the Composition Search Committee via email: compositionsearch@towson.edu Click here to apply. Please note that the search number for which you are applying is COFAC-4024. Please be sure to visit the Applicant Data Form to complete a voluntary on-line form. All data collected are for internal, state, and/or federal reporting and will not be used for other purposes. Salary and Benefits: Targeted salary range: $68,000-70,000 Benefits: TU offers a comprehensive benefits package that includes excellent health, life and retirement plans; and tuition remission. To learn more about our benefits, click here for regular faculty/regular lecturer or here for contingent lecturer. TU also offers a variety of great perks and discounts, which can be found here . Background Check: A criminal background investigation is required for the successful candidate, and results may affect employment. COVID-19 Statement: The safety of our students, faculty, staff, and neighbors has been our top priority and the focus of every one of our decisions since the earliest days of the COVID-19 pandemic. Therefore, the University System of Maryland (USM) has strongly encouraged full COVID vaccination and up-to-date booster shots (when eligible) for all faculty, staff, and students at all schools in the USM as both a reasonable and necessary means of protecting our health and safety. Organization : Academic Affairs Division Primary Location : Main Campus Job Posting : Sep 23, 2026 Towson University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. If you need a reasonable accommodation for any part of the employment process, please send an email to: adarequest@towson.edu Towson University is a smoke-free campus. \u00a92016 | 8000 York Road | Towson, MD 21252 | 410-704-2000"}, "https://towson.taleo.net/careersection/fac_ex/jobdetail.ftl?job=260000QL": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Music Theory", "description": "Job Description - Assistant Professor of Music Theory (260000QL) Go to the main content section. Welcome.  You are not signed in.  NOTE: If you experience any issues with this page, please contact the Towson University Office of Human Resources at 410-704-2162. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Assistant Professor of Music Theory (260000QL) Job Description Assistant Professor of Music Theory - ( 260000QL ) TU Search Number : COFAC 4025 Assistant Professor of Music Theory Department of Music College of Fine Arts and Communication COFAC-4025 Towson University: Towson University (TU) is one of the nation\u2019s top 100 public universities. Located north of Baltimore, TU currently enrolls over 19,000 students and is the second-largest university in the prestigious University System of Maryland. Towson University fosters a climate that is grounded in respect to cultivate the intellectual and personal growth of the entire university community. Position: The College of Fine Arts and Communication invites applications for a tenure-track, nine-month, full-time Assistant Professor of Music Theory in the Department of Music. The primary responsibility of this position is teaching music theory and musicianship. The Department seeks a student-centered educator able to bring professional experience and innovation to the undergraduate theory curriculum. Preferred candidates will be conversant with a wide range of musical practices and traditions. The p referred start date is August 2027. Qualifications: Applicants should hold a doctorate in music theory or a closely related field. ABD candidates will be considered but must have completed a doctoral degree prior to appointment. Candidates must demonstrate excellence in teaching theory and musicianship skills, a promising scholarly agenda, and capacity to serve the administrative needs of the Department of Music, the College of Fine Arts and Communication, and Towson University. Candidates with at least two years of university-level teaching experience are preferred. Responsibilities: Responsibilities of the position include 1) teaching undergraduate and graduate music theory and musicianship classes, with the possibility of contributing to the other areas of instruction based on candidate interest and experience; 2) maintaining a productive scholarly agenda consistent with Towson University\u2019s reputation for excellence in interdisciplinary research; 3) contributing to the development of an innovative music curriculum; 4) demonstrating meaningful commitment to inclusive pedagogy and student engagement; 5) serving on department, college, and university committees; 6) participating in departmental recruitment activities; and 7) student advising. The Department: The Department of Music serves a community of over 200 music majors and graduate students, as well as offering courses and performance opportunities to students specializing in other fields. Towson students engage in a range of rigorous scholarly, creative, and collaborative work that reflects a broad base of musical interests. Our students have the valuable opportunity to work with a music faculty including internationally recognized composers, performers, scholars, and public intellectuals who prioritize student achievement, scholarly skills, creativity, and community. The Department regularly hosts guest artists for masterclasses and guest lectures and has a long history of philanthropic support to sponsor the educational needs of its students. TU alumni are nationally and internationally renowned composers and performers, educators in PreK-12 and university settings, technological innovators, entrepreneurs, and arts administrators. The Department offers three undergraduate degree programs for music majors: the Bachelor of Science in Music, the Bachelor of Music (classical performance, jazz/commercial performance, or composition), and the Bachelor of Science in Music Education. The Department also offers minors in general music, music industry, jazz/commercial performance, and music technology. Graduate degrees include the Master of Science in Music Education, the Master of Music, the Master of Music in Music Pedagogy, and the Graduate Certificate in Applied Music. Application Process: Review of applications begins immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Priority will be given to applications completed by November 15, 2026. All materials must be submitted online through the university's application portal. A complete application portfolio includes 1) a letter of application addressing the candidate\u2019s qualifications for the position; 2) a curriculum vitae; 3) a statement of teaching philosophy; 4) a statement of current and future scholarly research; 5) a recent video demonstration of classroom teaching; 6) three letters of recommendation; and 7) unofficial transcripts from all institutions of higher education attended (official transcripts will be required at time of hire). Confidential letters of recommendation should be sent to musictheorysearch@towson.edu Note: Towson University is conducting a search for an Assistant Professor of Composition. Applicants wishing to be considered for both positions must submit a separate application for each. Enquiries should be addressed to the Theory Search Committee via email: musictheorysearch@towson.edu Click here to apply. Please note that the search number for which you are applying is COFAC-4025. Please be sure to visit the Applicant Data Form to complete a voluntary on-line form. All data collected are for internal, state, and/or federal reporting and will not be used for other purposes. Salary and Benefits: Targeted salary range: $68,000-70,000 Benefits: TU offers a comprehensive benefits package that includes excellent health, life and retirement plans; and tuition remission. To learn more about our benefits, click here for regular faculty/regular lecturer or here for contingent lecturer. TU also offers a variety of great perks and discounts, which can be found here . Background Check: A criminal background investigation is required for the successful candidate, and results may affect employment. COVID-19 Statement: The safety of our students, faculty, staff, and neighbors has been our top priority and the focus of every one of our decisions since the earliest days of the COVID-19 pandemic. Therefore, the University System of Maryland (USM) has strongly encouraged full COVID vaccination and up-to-date booster shots (when eligible) for all faculty, staff, and students at all schools in the USM as both a reasonable and necessary means of protecting our health and safety. Organization : Academic Affairs Division Primary Location : Main Campus Job Posting : Sep 28, 2026 Towson University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. If you need a reasonable accommodation for any part of the employment process, please send an email to: adarequest@towson.edu Towson University is a smoke-free campus. \u00a92016 | 8000 York Road | Towson, MD 21252 | 410-704-2000"}, "https://towson.taleo.net/careersection/fac_ex/jobdetail.ftl?job=260000PS": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Theatre", "description": "Job Description - Assistant Professor of Theatre (260000PS) Go to the main content section. Welcome.  You are not signed in.  NOTE: If you experience any issues with this page, please contact the Towson University Office of Human Resources at 410-704-2162. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Assistant Professor of Theatre (260000PS) Job Description Assistant Professor of Theatre - ( 260000PS ) TU Search Number : COFAC-4023 Assistant Professor Department of Theatre Arts College of Fine Arts and Communication COFAC-4023 Towson University: Towson University (TU) is one of the nation\u2019s top 100 public universities. Located north of Baltimore, TU currently enrolls over 19,000 students and is the second-largest university in the prestigious University System of Maryland. Towson University fosters a climate that is grounded in respect to cultivate the intellectual and personal growth of the entire university community. Position: The College of Fine Arts and Communications invites applications for a tenure-track, Assistant Professor position in the Department of Theatre Arts. This colleague will teach in the BFA in Acting track and help lead the program\u2019s growing musical theatre offerings, including the upcoming musical theatre minor. \u00a0Preferred start date August, 2027. Qualifications: Required: \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0MFA in Acting preferred, but related terminal degrees will be considered. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Demonstrated excellence teaching acting across both musical and non-musical performance. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Training in a recognized pedagogy of movement for the actor. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0A comprehensive view of the theatre discipline and the ability to teach and mentor students within a liberal arts education. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0A record of professional creative activity and/or scholarship. Ideal candidates will have experience engaging with theatre, including the development of new work, that reflects a broad range of communities, identities, and lived experiences, and demonstrates a commitment to inclusive artistic and educational practices. Skills in areas such as music direction or vocal coaching for singers are a welcome bonus, but they are not required, and candidates without them are encouraged to apply. Responsibilities: Faculty are assigned an instructional workload of 3/3, with primary responsibility for required courses in the BFA in Acting and reassigned time for directing and production responsibilities. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Ability to teach musical theatre courses, including Acting for Musical Theatre, Dance the Scene (Dance for the Actor), and Advanced Musical Theatre. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Ability to teach non-musical acting courses, including Acting I, Acting II, Intermediate Scene Study, and Movement I and II. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Direct productions in the mainstage season, as opportunities arise. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Support non-musical productions with dance and/or movement direction. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Collaborate with faculty in the Departments of Music and Dance to support and build the musical theatre program. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Advise and mentor student projects in areas such as new work development and educational outreach. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Support and contribute to the department\u2019s educational outreach efforts. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Participate actively in student recruitment and retention, including BFA auditions, college festivals, Unifieds, and outreach to prospective students, with particular attention to building the musical theatre program. This will include participation in musical theatre auditions once the minor is established. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Provide service to the department, college, university, and community. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Maintain an active record of creative activity and/or scholarship. The successful candidate will be a collaborative teaching artist committed to student creativity and success, able to teach across both musical and non-musical performance, and engaged in ongoing creative activity and/or scholarship. The Department: The Department of Theatre is housed within the College of Fine Arts and Communication and is dedicated to preparing emerging theatre artists through rigorous coursework, hands-on production experience, and engagement with professional practices. Students participate in a diverse production season and work closely with faculty who are active artists, scholars, and educators. Application Process: Review of applications begins immediately and continues until the position is filled. Applicants should submit: 1.\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Letter of application addressing qualifications for the position. 2.\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Curriculum vitae. 3.\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Statement of teaching philosophy. 4.\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Link to website or portfolio of creative work 5.\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Names and contact information for three professional references. All applicants must apply through Taleo** Click here to apply. Please note that the search number for which you are applying is COFAC-4023. Please be sure to visit the Applicant Data Form to complete a voluntary on-line form. All data collected are for internal, state, and/or federal reporting and will not be used for other purposes. Salary and Benefits: Targeted salary range: $67,000-70,000 commensurate with experience. Benefits: TU offers a comprehensive benefits package that includes excellent health, life and retirement plans; and tuition remission. To learn more about our benefits, click here for regular faculty/regular lecturer or here for contingent lecturer. TU also offers a variety of great perks and discounts, which can be found here. Background Check: A Criminal Background Investigation is required for the hired candidate and the results may impact employment. COVID-19 Statement: The safety of our students, faculty, staff, and neighbors has been our top priority and the focus of every one of our decisions since the earliest days of the COVID-19 pandemic. Therefore, the University System of Maryland (USM) has strongly encouraged full COVID vaccination and up-to-date booster shots (when eligible) for all faculty, staff, and students at all schools in the USM as both a reasonable and necessary means of protecting our health and safety. Salary and Benefits: Targeted salary range: $67,000-70,000 commensurate with experience. Benefits: TU offers a comprehensive benefits package that includes excellent health, life and retirement plans; and tuition remission. To learn more about our benefits, click here for regular faculty/regular lecturer or here for contingent lecturer. TU also offers a variety of great perks and discounts, which can be found here . Background Check: A Criminal Background Investigation is required for the hired candidate and the results may impact employment. COVID-19 Statement: The safety of our students, faculty, staff, and neighbors has been our top priority and the focus of every one of our decisions since the earliest days of the COVID-19 pandemic. Therefore, the University System of Maryland (USM) has strongly encouraged full COVID vaccination and up-to-date booster shots (when eligible) for all faculty, staff, and students at all schools in the USM as both a reasonable and necessary means of protecting our health and safety. Organization : Academic Affairs Division Primary Location : Main Campus Job Posting : Sep 23, 2026 Towson University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. If you need a reasonable accommodation for any part of the employment process, please send an email to: adarequest@towson.edu Towson University is a smoke-free campus. \u00a92016 | 8000 York Road | Towson, MD 21252 | 410-704-2000"}, "https://towson.taleo.net/careersection/fac_ex/jobdetail.ftl?job=260000RF": {"title": "Assistant Teaching Professor", "description": "Job Description - Assistant Teaching Professor (260000RF) Go to the main content section. Welcome.  You are not signed in.  NOTE: If you experience any issues with this page, please contact the Towson University Office of Human Resources at 410-704-2162. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Assistant Teaching Professor (260000RF) Job Description Assistant Teaching Professor - ( 260000RF ) TU Search Number : COFAC-4028L Towson University: Towson University (TU) is one of the nation\u2019s top 100 public universities. Located north of Baltimore, TU currently enrolls over 19,000 students and is the second-largest university in the prestigious University System of Maryland. Towson University fosters a climate that is grounded in respect to cultivate the intellectual and personal growth of the entire university community. Position: Towson University invites applications for a Teaching Professor position in the department of Theatre Arts, in the area of Costume Design. Preferred start date, August 2027. Qualifications: MFA in Costume Design, Costume Technology, or a closely related field. Demonstrated expertise in costume design and visual storytelling for theatrical production. E vidence of successful teaching, mentoring, or professional training experience. Commitment to student-centered teaching and mentorship. Ability to work effectively with colleagues, students, and community partners from diverse backgrounds. Preferred Qualifications: University-level teaching experience. Experience mentoring student designers in production settings. Professional regional, commercial, educational, dance, opera, or film/television design experience. Experience incorporating emerging technologies and digital design tools into teaching and creative practice. Responsibilities: T he successful candidate will teach undergraduate courses in Costume Design and related areas, including but not limited to costume design, costume construction, costume history, costume crafts, rendering, and portfolio development. A 4/4 load is expected, with a course release for designing/mentoring student designers per semester. Additional responsibilities may include: Mentoring and supervising student costume designers and costume technicians for departmental productions. Collaborating with faculty and production staff on the department's production season. Participating in departmental, college, and university service appropriate to the rank of Teaching Professor The Department: The Department of Theatre is a dynamic and collaborative community of artists, scholars, and educators committed to preparing students for professional careers and advanced study in theatre. The department offers undergraduate programs in Performance, Design and Production and Theatre Studies, and supports an active production season that serves as a central component of student learning. Faculty members maintain significant professional and creative activity while mentoring students in classroom and production environments. Application Process: Review of applications begins immediately and continues until the position is filled. Applicants should submit: Letter of application addressing qualifications for the position. Curriculum vitae. Statement of teaching philosophy. Portfolio of professional and/or creative work. Names and contact information for three professional references. Please note that the search number for which you are applying is COFAC-4028L. Please be sure to visit the Applicant Data Form to complete a voluntary on-line form. All data collected are for internal, state, and/or federal reporting and will not be used for other purposes. Salary and Benefits: Targeted salary: $58,000-$64,000 Benefits: TU offers a comprehensive benefits package that includes excellent health, life and retirement plans; and tuition remission. To learn more about our benefits, click here for regular faculty/regular lecturer or here for contingent lecturer. TU also offers a variety of great perks and discounts, which can be found here . Background Check: A Criminal Background Investigation is required for the hired candidate and the results may impact employment. COVID-19 Statement: The safety of our students, faculty, staff, and neighbors has been our top priority and the focus of every one of our decisions since the earliest days of the COVID-19 pandemic. Therefore, the University System of Maryland (USM) has strongly encouraged full COVID vaccination and up-to-date booster shots (when eligible) for all faculty, staff, and students at all schools in the USM as both a reasonable and necessary means of protecting our health and safety. Organization : Academic Affairs Division Primary Location : Main Campus Job Posting : Oct 12, 2026 Towson University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. If you need a reasonable accommodation for any part of the employment process, please send an email to: adarequest@towson.edu Towson University is a smoke-free campus. \u00a92016 | 8000 York Road | Towson, MD 21252 | 410-704-2000"}, "https://towson.taleo.net/careersection/fac_ex/jobdetail.ftl?job=260000M8": {"title": "Assistant Professor, Biomechanics", "description": "Job Description - Assistant Professor, Biomechanics (260000M8) Go to the main content section. Welcome.  You are not signed in.  NOTE: If you experience any issues with this page, please contact the Towson University Office of Human Resources at 410-704-2162. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Assistant Professor, Biomechanics (260000M8) Job Description Assistant Professor, Biomechanics - ( 260000M8 ) TU Search Number : CHP-4014 Assistant Professor, Biomechanics Department of Kinesiology College of Health Professions CHP-4014 Position : The College of Health Professions invites applications for a tenure-track, 9-month Assistant Professor position in the Department of Kinesiology. Preferred start date is August, 2027. Qualifications : Research doctoral degree in Exercise Science or closely related field. ABD applicants considered, but appointment will be at the Instructor rank and all degree requirements must be completed by February 1, 2028. Candidates must present evidence of a scholarship agenda focused in an area of specialty in Exercise Science that complements the expertise of current faculty, the course offerings, and available resources. Human subjects research with potential for external funding is highly valued. Candidates must have the training and expertise to teach multiple Exercise Science courses in the following areas: biomechanics, motor learning, motor development, and/or research methods. Candidates with expertise to teach across the kinesiology disciplinary boundaries are highly valued and encouraged to apply. Post-doctoral candidates are encouraged to apply. Responsibilities: Primary responsibilities include: 1) Teaching \u2013 research-active instructors teach 6 units (typically, 3 courses per semester) over a 9- month academic year in a highly diverse, student-centered program; provide high-quality instruction in a variety of kinesiology courses; advise and mentor students as they matriculate through the program and prepare to enter the profession; 2) Scholarship \u2013 development/continuation of a focused area of scholarship that includes refereed publications, professional presentations, external funding, and involvement in scholarly projects with faculty and students; 3) Service \u2013 active service participation at the department, college, university, profession and community levels. Department Information: The Department of Kinesiology, located within the College of Health Professions, has over 30 full-time faculty and more than 1,000 students across the Health and Physical Education, Sport Management, Fitness and Wellness Leadership, and Exercise Science undergraduate programs. The Department also offers a Master\u2019s degree in Athletic Training. All programs value success in working with diverse populations and students. The Department of Kinesiology maintains a strong, positive working relationship with the University\u2019s Division of Athletics and Campus Recreation. Towson University: Towson University (TU) is one of the nation\u2019s top 100 public universities. Located north of Baltimore, TU currently enrolls over 19,000 students and is the second-largest university in the prestigious University System of Maryland. Towson University fosters a climate that is grounded in respect to cultivate the intellectual and personal growth of the entire university community. Application Process: Review of applications begins immediately and continues until the position is filled. Interested applicants should submit a letter of application that addresses the posting details and qualifications. Applications must also include: (1) a curriculum vitae, (2) a teaching statement, (3) a research statement that addresses current areas of expertise and future research agenda, and (4) contact information (name, address, email, phone number) for at least three professional references. All application materials should be submitted electronically via the application link, preferably in a single PDF file. Click here to apply. Please note that the search number for which you are applying is CHP-4014. Please be sure to visit the Applicant Data Form to complete a voluntary on-line form. All data collected are for internal, state, and/or federal reporting and will not be used for other purposes. Salary and Benefits: Targeted salary range: $80,000-$85,000 commensurate with experience. Benefits: TU offers a comprehensive benefits package that includes excellent health, life and retirement plans; and tuition remission. To learn more about our benefits, click here for regular faculty/regular lecturer or here for contingent lecturer. TU also offers a variety of great perks and discounts, which can be found here . Background Check: A Criminal Background Investigation is required for the hired candidate and the results may impact employment. COVID-19 Statement: The safety of our students, faculty, staff, and neighbors has been our top priority and the focus of every one of our decisions since the earliest days of the COVID-19 pandemic. Therefore, the University System of Maryland (USM) has strongly encouraged full COVID vaccination and up-to-date booster shots (when eligible) for all faculty, staff, and students at all schools in the USM as both a reasonable and necessary means of protecting our health and safety. Organization : Academic Affairs Division Primary Location : Main Campus Job Posting : Aug 18, 2026 Towson University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. If you need a reasonable accommodation for any part of the employment process, please send an email to: adarequest@towson.edu Towson University is a smoke-free campus. \u00a92016 | 8000 York Road | Towson, MD 21252 | 410-704-2000"}, "https://towson.taleo.net/careersection/fac_ex/jobdetail.ftl?job=260000M9": {"title": "Assistant Professor, Sport and Performance Analytics", "description": "Job Description - Assistant Professor, Sport and Performance Analytics (260000M9) Go to the main content section. Welcome.  You are not signed in.  NOTE: If you experience any issues with this page, please contact the Towson University Office of Human Resources at 410-704-2162. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Assistant Professor, Sport and Performance Analytics (260000M9) Job Description Assistant Professor, Sport and Performance Analytics - ( 260000M9 ) TU Search Number : CHP-4015 Assistant Professor, Sport and Performance Analytics Department of Kinesiology College of Health Professions CHP-4015 Position : The College of Health Professions invites applications for a tenure-track, 9-month Assistant Professor position in the Department of Kinesiology. Preferred start date is August, 2027. Qualifications : Research doctoral degree in Exercise Science or related field. ABD applicants considered, but appointment will be at the Instructor rank and all degree requirements must be completed by February 1, 2028. Candidates must present evidence of a scholarship agenda focused in an area of specialty in Exercise Science that complements the expertise of current faculty, the course offerings, and available resources. Human subjects research with potential for external funding is highly valued. Candidates must have the training and expertise to teach multiple Exercise Science courses in the following areas: sports and performance analytics, data analytics, athlete monitoring, quantitative research methods, strength and conditioning, and/or athletic training . Candidates with Certified Strength and Conditioning Specialist (CSCS) and/or Certified Performance and Sport Scientist (CPSS) certifications are highly valued and encouraged to apply. Candidates with expertise to teach across the kinesiology disciplinary boundaries are highly valued and encouraged to apply. Postdoctoral candidates are encouraged to apply. Responsibilities: Primary responsibilities include: 1) Teaching \u2013 research-active instructors teach 6 units (typically, 3 courses per semester) over a 9- month academic year in a highly diverse, student-centered program; provide high-quality instruction in a variety of kinesiology courses; advise and mentor students as they matriculate through the program and prepare to enter the profession; 2) Scholarship \u2013 development/continuation of a focused area of scholarship that includes refereed publications, professional presentations, external funding, and involvement in scholarly projects with faculty and students; 3) Service \u2013 active service participation at the department, college, university, profession and community levels. Department Information: The Department of Kinesiology, located within the College of Health Professions, has over 30 full-time faculty and more than 1,000 students across the Health and Physical Education, Sport Management, Fitness and Wellness Leadership, and Exercise Science undergraduate programs. The Department also offers a Master\u2019s degree in Athletic Training. All programs value success in working with diverse populations and students. The Department of Kinesiology maintains a strong, positive working relationship with the University\u2019s Division of Athletics and Campus Recreation. Towson University: Towson University (TU) is one of the nation\u2019s top 100 public universities. Located north of Baltimore, TU currently enrolls over 19,000 students and is the second-largest university in the prestigious University System of Maryland. Towson University fosters a climate that is grounded in respect to cultivate the intellectual and personal growth of the entire university community. Application Process: Review of applications begins immediately and continues until the position is filled. Interested applicants should submit a letter of application that addresses the posting details and qualifications. Applications must also include: (1) a curriculum vitae, (2) a teaching statement, (3) a research statement that addresses current areas of expertise and future research agenda, and (4) contact information (name, address, email, phone number) for at least three professional references. All application materials should be submitted electronically via the application link, preferably in a single PDF file. Click here to apply. Please note that the search number for which you are applying is CHP-4015. Please be sure to visit the Applicant Data Form to complete a voluntary on-line form. All data collected are for internal, state, and/or federal reporting and will not be used for other purposes. Salary and Benefits: Targeted salary range: $80,000-$85,000 commensurate with experience. Benefits: TU offers a comprehensive benefits package that includes excellent health, life and retirement plans; and tuition remission. To learn more about our benefits, click here for regular faculty/regular lecturer or here for contingent lecturer. TU also offers a variety of great perks and discounts, which can be found here . Background Check: A Criminal Background Investigation is required for the hired candidate and the results may impact employment. COVID-19 Statement: The safety of our students, faculty, staff, and neighbors has been our top priority and the focus of every one of our decisions since the earliest days of the COVID-19 pandemic. Therefore, the University System of Maryland (USM) has strongly encouraged full COVID vaccination and up-to-date booster shots (when eligible) for all faculty, staff, and students at all schools in the USM as both a reasonable and necessary means of protecting our health and safety. Organization : Academic Affairs Division Primary Location : Main Campus Job Posting : Aug 18, 2026 Towson University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. If you need a reasonable accommodation for any part of the employment process, please send an email to: adarequest@towson.edu Towson University is a smoke-free campus. \u00a92016 | 8000 York Road | Towson, MD 21252 | 410-704-2000"}, "https://towson.taleo.net/careersection/fac_ex/jobdetail.ftl?job=260000ON": {"title": "Assistant or Associate Professor in Nursing", "description": "Job Description - Assistant or Associate Professor in Nursing (260000ON) Go to the main content section. Welcome.  You are not signed in.  NOTE: If you experience any issues with this page, please contact the Towson University Office of Human Resources at 410-704-2162. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Assistant or Associate Professor in Nursing (260000ON) Job Description Assistant or Associate Professor in Nursing - ( 260000ON ) TU Search Number : CHP-4018 Assistant Professor or Associate Professor College of Health Professions Department of Nursing CHP-4018 Towson University: Towson University (TU) is one of the nation\u2019s top 100 public universities. Located north of Baltimore, TU currently enrolls over 19,000 students and is the second-largest university in the prestigious University System of Maryland. Towson University fosters a climate that is grounded in respect to cultivating the intellectual and personal growth of the entire university community. Position: The College of Health Professions invites applications for three full-time, nine-month tenure-track faculty positions at the Assistant or Associate Professor rank in the Department of Nursing. Preferred begin date, August 2027. Qualifications: A research doctorate (excludes clinical practice doctorate) with expertise in a respective specialty area is required. Evidence of an active research agenda is also required. Candidates should have experience working with diverse populations. ABD applicants will be considered, with appointment at the instructor rank; all degree requirements must be completed by February 1, 2028. Candidates must hold a current unencumbered Maryland RN license or be eligible for Maryland RN licensure and demonstrate a commitment to excellence in teaching and advising. Salary is competitive and commensurate with experience. Candidates seeking appointment at the Associate Professor rank should have six years of higher education teaching experience or comparable qualifications and demonstrate a clear line of research with documented scholarly outcomes. Responsibilities: 1)Teaching - provide high quality instruction in a variety of undergraduate and/or graduate nursing courses to a diverse group of students, advise and mentor students as they matriculate through the program and prepare to enter the profession; 2) Scholarship \u2013 pursue, contribute to and/or collaborate with colleagues in scholarship that reflects one\u2019s area of specialization ; this may include publications, quality improvement projects and grant related initiatives; 3) Service \u2013 actively participate in service at the Department, College, University, professional and community levels. The Department: The Department of Nursing is one of five academic units within the College of Health Professions. Accredited by the Commission on Collegiate Nursing Education (CCNE), the department enrolls approximately 600 pre-licensure undergraduate students, including those in the Associate-to-Bachelor\u2019s degree program, and approximately 35 students in the Entry-Level Master of Science in Nursing program. Application Process: Review of completed applications begins immediately and continues until the position is filled. Applicants should submit a letter of application, current curriculum vitae, proof of unencumbered RN license, contact information for professional references and an official graduate transcript. Application materials should be submitted electronically via the application link, preferably in a single PDF file. Click here to apply. Please note that the search number for which you are applying is CHP-4018 Please be sure to visit the Applicant Data Form to complete a voluntary on-line form. All data collected are for internal, state, and/or federal reporting and will not be used for other purposes. Salary and Benefits: Targeted salary range: $86,000-$91,000 salary range for Assistant Professor / $105,000-$110,000 salary range for Associate Professor. Salary range commensurate with experience. Benefits: TU offers a comprehensive benefits package that includes excellent health, life and retirement plans; and tuition remission. To learn more about our benefits, click here for regular faculty/regular lecturer or here for contingent lecturer. TU also offers a variety of great perks and discounts, which can be found here . Background Check: A Criminal Background Investigation is required for the hired candidate and the results may impact employment. COVID-19 Statement: The safety of our students, faculty, staff, and neighbors has been our top priority and the focus of every one of our decisions since the earliest days of the COVID-19 pandemic. Therefore, the University System of Maryland (USM) has strongly encouraged full COVID vaccination and up-to-date booster shots (when eligible) for all faculty, staff, and students at all schools in the USM as both a reasonable and necessary means of protecting our health and safety. Organization : Academic Affairs Division Primary Location : Main Campus Job Posting : Sep 11, 2026 Towson University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. If you need a reasonable accommodation for any part of the employment process, please send an email to: adarequest@towson.edu Towson University is a smoke-free campus. \u00a92016 | 8000 York Road | Towson, MD 21252 | 410-704-2000"}, "https://towson.taleo.net/careersection/fac_ex/jobdetail.ftl?job=260000OP": {"title": "Assistant or Associate Professor", "description": "Job Description - Assistant or Associate Professor (260000OP) Go to the main content section. Welcome.  You are not signed in.  NOTE: If you experience any issues with this page, please contact the Towson University Office of Human Resources at 410-704-2162. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Assistant or Associate Professor (260000OP) Job Description Assistant or Associate Professor - ( 260000OP ) TU Search Number : CHP 4017 Assistant or Associate Professor Department of Occupational Therapy and Occupational Science College of Health Professions CHP-4017 Towson University: Towson University (TU) is one of the nation\u2019s top 100 public universities. Located north of Baltimore, TU currently enrolls over 19,000 students and is the second-largest university in the prestigious University System of Maryland. Towson University fosters a climate that is grounded in respect to cultivate the intellectual and personal growth of the entire university community. Position: The College of Health Professions invites applications for a tenure-track, 9-month Assistant Professor or Associate Professor position in the Department of Occupational Therapy and Occupational Science. Preferred begin date, August 2027. Qualifications: Earned research doctoral degree by February 28, 2028. Licensed or eligible for licensure as an occupational therapist in the State of Maryland; teaching experience in occupational therapy or occupational science; and active research agenda with capacity for scholarly productivity and external funding. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills. Demonstrated awareness and clear articulation of strategies to foster an inclusive learning environment. Commitment to excellence in teaching, advising, scholarship, and service. Salary is commensurate with experience and rank; ABD candidates will be hired at the rank of instructor until doctoral degree is completed. Candidates wishing to be considered for the rank of Associate Professor should have 6 years of experience teaching in higher education or comparable qualifications, and demonstrate a clear line of research with scholarly outcomes. Responsibilities: Primary responsibilities include Teaching: Facilitate classroom and applied learning experiences for diverse graduate professional students in occupational therapy and occupational science, advise and mentor students, and direct student research at the doctoral level. Scholarship: Conduct and disseminate research and seek external funding to support focused area of inquiry. Service: Participate in active service to the department, college, university, community, and profession. The Department: The vision of the Department of Occupational Therapy and Occupational Science is to be a national leader in the development of occupational therapy practitioners and occupational scientists who improve the health and occupational lives of individuals, communities and populations. The department values innovative teaching, active learning experiences, community-engaged research and dynamic community partnerships. Towson University is situated within proximity to nationally renowned medical centers and healthcare resources, with many opportunities to research and support best practices in occupational therapy. The College of Health Professions\u2019 Institute for Wellbeing offers extensive opportunities for research, community outreach and program evaluation, including the Occupational Therapy Center and the Hussman Center for Adults with Autism. Application Process: Review of completed application begins immediately and continues until the position is filled. Interested applicants should submit a letter of application that addresses the posting details and qualifications. Applications must also include: (1) a curriculum vitae, (2) a teaching statement that includes descriptions of teaching philosophy, practical approaches, and a list of potential course offerings, and (3) a research statement that addresses current areas of expertise and future research agenda. The names and addresses (including email addresses) of three (3) references should be provided, including at least one who can speak directly to teaching quality and experience. ABD applicants should provide evidence of doctoral progress, such as date of final defense or letter from Committee Chair. Click here to apply. Please note the search number for which you are applying is CHP-4017. Please be sure to visit the Applicant Data Form to complete a voluntary on-line form. All data collected are for internal, state, and/or federal reporting and will not be used for other purposes. Salary and Benefits Targeted salary range: $84,000-87,000 commensurate with experience for Assistant Professor; $92,000-98,000 commensurate with experience for Associate Professor. Benefits: TU offers a comprehensive benefits package that includes excellent health, life and retirement plans; and tuition remission. To learn more about our benefits, click here for regular faculty/regular lecturer or here for contingent lecturer. TU also offers a variety of great perks and discounts, which can be found here. Background Check: A Criminal Background Investigation is required for the hired candidate and the results may impact employment. COVID-19 Statement: The safety of our students, faculty, staff, and neighbors has been our top priority and the focus of every one of our decisions since the earliest days of the COVID-19 pandemic. Therefore, the University System of Maryland (USM) has strongly encouraged full COVID vaccination and up to-date booster shots (when eligible) for all faculty, staff, and students at all schools in the USM as both a reasonable and necessary means of protecting our health and safety. Organization : Academic Affairs Division Primary Location : Main Campus Job Posting : Sep 14, 2026 Towson University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. If you need a reasonable accommodation for any part of the employment process, please send an email to: adarequest@towson.edu Towson University is a smoke-free campus. \u00a92016 | 8000 York Road | Towson, MD 21252 | 410-704-2000"}, "https://towson.taleo.net/careersection/fac_ex/jobdetail.ftl?job=2600008E": {"title": "Clinical Assistant Professor or Clinical Associate Professor", "description": "Job Description - Clinical Assistant Professor or Clinical Associate Professor (2600008E) Go to the main content section. Welcome.  You are not signed in.  NOTE: If you experience any issues with this page, please contact the Towson University Office of Human Resources at 410-704-2162. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Clinical Assistant Professor or Clinical Associate Professor (2600008E) Job Description Clinical Assistant Professor or Clinical Associate Professor - ( 2600008E ) TU Search Number : CHP-3919 Clinical Assistant Professor or Clinical Associate Professor Department of Physician Assistant Studies College of Health Professions CHP-3919 Position: The College of Health Professions at Towson University invites applications for two (2) non-tenure-track, 12-month position at the Clinical Assistant or Clinical Associate Professor rank in the Department of Physician Assistant Studies beginning Spring 2026. Qualifications: A minimum of an accredited Physician Assistant Studies master\u2019s degree (or its equivalent) with NCCPA certification and eligibility for licensure in the state of Maryland at the time of appointment. A minimum of three years of clinical or professional experience. Ability and willingness to teach a range of Physician Assistant related didactic and clinical courses. Excellent professional, written, oral, and conceptual skills. Commitment to collaborating with a wide variety of faculty, students, and staff to foster and enhance a supportive successful teaching environment. Candidates wanting to be considered for the rank of clinical associate professor should have a minimum of 3 years of full-time higher education experience, 3 years of teaching experience, a record of service, and scholarly works. Responsibilities: Primary responsibilities include delivery of high-quality instruction in various Physician Assistant courses and mentoring and advising students as they matriculate through the program. The expected workload is an equivalent of 80% teaching across the semesters, ongoing professional development and education while maintaining clinical expertise. Candidates are also encouraged to engage in traditional scholarship activities that may include publishing, professional presentations, and collaborative scholarly projects that may include external funding. Faculty participate in service activities at the Department, College, University, Profession, and community levels. All faculty are expected to meet ARC-PA standards and essential program faculty functions. ESSENTIAL PROGRAM FACULTY FUNCTIONS \u2013 Participate in curricular design, implementation and review of mission, program goals and the effectiveness of any changes. Selecting applicants for admission to the PA program. Participate in ongoing Program evaluation. Provide learning experiences through teaching and supervision for students in the didactic and clinical phases of the PA program. Provide an evaluation of student performance, as related to the objectives of the courses and program. Participate in review of program compliance with ARC-PA standards, policies and procedures. Advise, counsel and mentor PA students. Assuring the availability of remedial instruction. Participate in service activities, including committee work and community outreach. Maintain a high level of clinical and professional excellence. ADDITIONAL LEADERSHIP OPPORTUNITIES \u2013 Based on interest and expertise, eligible candidates may be assigned program related leadership responsibilities to include: Director of Clinical Education-Develop and manage supervised clinical practice experiences for clinical year students by collaborating with existing clinical partners \u00a0and developing new clinical placements. Director of Student Success-the individual would be responsible for early identification of students at risk and developing remediation activities. Director of Accreditation & Assessment-the individual would be responsible for managing the annual program evaluation and assessment plan to meet ARC-PA Standards. Associate Program Director-Support the Program Director in the administration, accreditation compliance, curriculum oversight, faculty coordination, and student progression processes to ensure effective delivery of high-quality education Responsibilities adapted from TU Policy 02-01.00, \u00a7 VI.B.3.c.ii, ARC-PA Standards (6th Edition) A2.05, a-h, and CHP Guidelines \u00a7 IV.A.1-6 Department and Program Information: The Department of Physician Assistant Studies is one of the six academic departments in the Towson University College of Health Professions. In addition to the Chair/ Program Director, the program is comprised of full-time faculty, part-time faculty, and staff positions. The program is 26 months long, beginning in June, and is approved by the ARC-PA for up to 36 students, annually. One of the oldest in the country, the program has Accreditation-Continued status to the Towson University Department of\u00a0Physician Assistant Studies Program sponsored by Towson\u00a0University . Accreditation-Continued is an accreditation status granted when a currently accredited program is in compliance with the ARC-PA Standards . The approximate date for the next validation review of the program by the ARC-PA will be October 2033 . The review date is contingent upon continued compliance with the Accreditation Standards and ARC-PA policy. The program\u2019s accreditation history can be viewed on the ARC-PA website at https://www.arc-pa.org/accreditation-history-towson-university/ . Towson University: Towson University ( https://www.towson.edu/ ) was founded in 1866, is recognized by U.S. News and World Reports as one of the top public universities in the Northeast and Mid-Atlantic regions, is Baltimore\u2019s largest university, and is the largest public, comprehensive institution in the University of Maryland System. TU enrolls over 19,000 undergraduates and more than 3,000 graduate students across six academic colleges (business, education, fine arts, health professions, liberal arts, science & mathematics), has 900 full-time faculty, and offers 65 bachelor\u2019s 42 master\u2019s, and 4 doctoral programs. Our centrally located campus sits on 330 rolling green acres and is 10 miles north of Baltimore, 45 miles north of Washington D.C., and 95 miles south of Philadelphia. Application Process: Review of applications begins immediately and continues until the positions are filled. Preliminary interviews may be conducted via phone or Zoom. The second interview will follow thereafter in person with key faculty members within the department and the College of Health Professions. For full consideration, a Curriculum Vitae, cover letter, and transcripts must be included in your application. Please identify potential interest in leadership and the Additional Opportunities. Click here ( INSERT TALEO LINK HERE ) to apply. Please note that the search number for which you are applying is CHP-3919. Please be sure to visit the Applicant Data Form ( https://www.towson.edu/inclusionequity/diversity/employment/data.html ) to complete a voluntary online form. All data collected are for internal, state, and/or federal reporting and will not be used for other purposes. Salary and Benefits: Targeted Salary Range: $120,000-$130,000 Clinical Assistant Professor; $135,000-$150,000 Clinical Associate Professor, commensurate with experience and responsibilities. Benefits: TU offers a comprehensive benefits package that includes excellent health, life and retirement plans; and tuition remission. To learn more about our benefits, click here ( https://www.towson.edu/hr/documents/benefits_summary_faculty.pdf ) for regular faculty/regular lecturers or here\u00a0( https://www.towson.edu/hr/documents/benefits_summary_lecturers.pdf ) for contingent lecturer. Towson University also offers a variety of great perks and discounts, which can be found here ( https://www.towson.edu/hr/current/benefits/perks-discounts.html ). Background Check: A Criminal Background Investigation is required for the hired candidate, and the results may impact employment. COVID-19 Statement: The safety of our students, faculty, staff, and neighbors has been our top priority and the focus of every one of our decisions since the earliest days of the COVID-19 pandemic. Therefore, the University System of Maryland (USM) has strongly encouraged full COVID vaccination and up-to-date booster shots (when eligible) for all faculty, staff, and students at all schools in the USM as both a reasonable and necessary means of protecting our health and safety. Organization : Academic Affairs Division Primary Location : Main Campus Job Posting : Apr 1, 2026 Towson University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. If you need a reasonable accommodation for any part of the employment process, please send an email to: adarequest@towson.edu Towson University is a smoke-free campus. \u00a92016 | 8000 York Road | Towson, MD 21252 | 410-704-2000"}, "https://towson.taleo.net/careersection/fac_ex/jobdetail.ftl?job=260000M7": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Speech-Language Pathology", "description": "Job Description - Assistant Professor of Speech-Language Pathology (260000M7) Go to the main content section. Welcome.  You are not signed in.  NOTE: If you experience any issues with this page, please contact the Towson University Office of Human Resources at 410-704-2162. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Assistant Professor of Speech-Language Pathology (260000M7) Job Description Assistant Professor of Speech-Language Pathology - ( 260000M7 ) TU Search Number : CHP-4010 Assistant Professor in Speech-Language Pathology Department of Speech-Language Pathology & Audiology Autism Studies PhD Program College of Health Professions CHP-4010 Towson University: Towson University (TU) is one of the nation\u2019s top 100 public universities. Located north of Baltimore, TU currently enrolls over 19,000 students and is the second-largest university in the prestigious University System of Maryland. Towson University fosters a climate that is grounded in respect to cultivate the intellectual and personal growth of the entire university community. Position: The College of Health Professions invites applications for a tenure-track, 9-month Assistant Professor position in the Department of Speech-Language Pathology & Audiology and in affiliation with the interdisciplinary Autism Studies PhD program in the College of Health Professions. Preferred begin date is August 2027. Faculty with expertise in autism are encouraged to apply. Qualifications: Applicants should have a doctoral degree in speech-language pathology or a related field. ABD applications will be considered with initial appointment at the Instructor rank; all degree requirements must be completed by February 28, 2028. Candidates should have a commitment to working across programs, disciplines, and cultures to strengthen the field. Candidates with ASHA CCC-SLP certification and current (or eligibility for) Maryland licensure will be prioritized. Responsibilities: Primary responsibilities include: (1) Teaching: Research-active instructors teach 6 course units (equivalent to 18 credits) over a 9-month academic year in our student-focused programs, providing high-quality instruction at the undergraduate and graduate levels, and advising and mentoring students as they matriculate through the associated programs and prepare to enter the profession (clinical supervision and Autism Studies PhD student mentorship also included in this position); (2) Scholarship: Development/continuation of a focused area of research that includes peer-reviewed publications, professional presentations, grant funding, and involvement in scholarly projects with students, and involvement of doctoral students/mentees; and (3) Service: Active service participation at the department, college, university, community, and professional levels. The Department: The Department of Speech-Language Pathology & Audiology currently has 19 full-time faculty who teach nearly 150 undergraduate students, over 100 master\u2019s students in Speech-Language Pathology, and over 60 students in an Audiology clinical doctorate program. The College of Health Professions is also home to a unique interdisciplinary Autism Studies PhD program with over 14 affiliated faculty and a growing number of students from various disciplinary backgrounds. The Autism Studies PhD program focuses on preparing leaders in the field of autism research and advocacy. Affiliated faculty serve as doctoral research mentors and engage with the program through various service opportunities. The Department and PhD program value culture, belonging, community, and interdisciplinary engagement. The Department is the academic home to two clinical and outreach centers, the Speech & Language Center and the Hearing & Balance Center; these two centers are part of the College\u2019s Institute for Well-Being (IWB), which is the University\u2019s premiere interprofessional education and practice center. The IWB also houses the Hussman Center for Adults with Autism, which partners with the Autism Studies faculty and students on research and practice. Application Process : Review of applications begins immediately and continues until the positions are filled. Interested applicants should submit a letter of application that addresses the posting details and qualifications. Applications should also include: (1) curriculum vitae, (2) teaching statement, (3) research statement that addresses current and future research agenda, (4) three letters of recommendation, and (5) contact information (name, address, email, phone number) for three professional references (may be those who wrote letters of recommendation). Application materials should be submitted electronically via the application link, preferably in a single PDF file. Questions should be directed to the Chair of the search committee: Kaitlyn Wilson, Ph.D., Chair of Faculty Search Committee Department of Speech-Language Pathology & Audiology Autism Studies PhD Program Towson University kwilson@towson.edu 410-704-5375 Please click here to apply. Please note that the search number for which you are applying is CHP-4010. Please be sure to visit the Applicant Data Form to complete a voluntary on-line form. All data collected are for internal, state, and/or federal reporting and will not be used for other purposes. Salary and Benefits: Targeted salary range: $83,000 - $88,000 commensurate with experience. Benefits: TU offers a comprehensive benefits package that includes excellent health, life and retirement plans; and tuition remission. To learn more about our benefits, click here for regular faculty/teaching professor or here for contingent teaching professor. TU also offers a variety of great perks and discounts, which can be found here . Background Check: A Criminal Background Investigation is required for the hired candidate, and the results may impact employment. COVID-19 Statement: The safety of our students, faculty, staff, and neighbors has been our top priority and the focus of every one of our decisions since the earliest days of the COVID-19 pandemic. Therefore, the University System of Maryland (USM) has strongly encouraged full COVID vaccination and up-to-date booster shots (when eligible) for all faculty, staff, and students at all schools in the USM as both a reasonable and necessary means of protecting our health and safety. Organization : Academic Affairs Division Primary Location : Main Campus Job Posting : Aug 15, 2026 Towson University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. If you need a reasonable accommodation for any part of the employment process, please send an email to: adarequest@towson.edu Towson University is a smoke-free campus. \u00a92016 | 8000 York Road | Towson, MD 21252 | 410-704-2000"}, "https://towson.taleo.net/careersection/fac_ex/jobdetail.ftl?job=260000LJ": {"title": "Assistant Professor of English", "description": "Job Description - Assistant Professor of English (260000LJ) Go to the main content section. Welcome.  You are not signed in.  NOTE: If you experience any issues with this page, please contact the Towson University Office of Human Resources at 410-704-2162. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Assistant Professor of English (260000LJ) Job Description Assistant Professor of English - ( 260000LJ ) TU Search Number : CLA-4013 Assistant Professor Department of English College of Liberal Arts CLA-4013 Towson University: Towson University (TU) is one of the nation\u2019s top 100 public universities. Located north of Baltimore, TU currently enrolls over 19,000 students and is the second-largest university in the prestigious University System of Maryland. Towson University fosters a climate that is grounded in respect to cultivate the intellectual and personal growth of the entire university community. Position: The College of Liberal Arts invites applications for a n assistant professor position in the English Department. Preferred start date is August 18, 2027. Qualifications: Applicants must have a terminal degree in creative writing (MFA or PhD) or related field, and a strong record of high-quality fiction publications or promise thereof and demonstrated excellence as a teacher. Expertise in other areas related to professional writing\u2014such as editing, magazine production, freelance writing, or other types of creative writing\u2014is desirable. Responsibilities: 2/3 courseload in the first year, followed by 3/3 courseload ranging from introductory level to classes in our graduate professional writing program, and rotations teaching Editing the Literary Magazine; advise 10-15 undergraduates. Applicants will need to demonstrate the potential for strong research, excellent teaching, and service aligned with the college\u2019s expected outcomes of impact, innovation, and engagement toward R2 status and the university\u2019s strategic plan: Leadership for the Public Good. The Department: The Department of English serves all students at the university through extensive general education offerings that strive to improve writing skills, expand liberal learning, and focus critical and analytic thinking. In addition, the English major supports the university\u2019s areas of emphasis in teacher education, public and private sector development and service, and liberal education. The department\u2019s graduate program in professional writing , unique in Maryland and paralleled by only six other programs nationwide, graduates writers who meet the needs of government and social and commercial organizations that rely on expert and efficient writing. Application Process: Review of applications begins immediately and continues until the position is filled, with priority given to those received by Nov. 2. To apply, send: cv, cover letter, statement of teaching philosophy, sample syllabus, and a writing sample of no more than 25 pages. Click here to apply. Please note that the search number for which you are applying is CLA-4013 . Please be sure to visit the Applicant Data Form to complete a voluntary on-line form. All data collected are for internal, state, and/or federal reporting and will not be used for other purposes. Salary and Benefits: Targeted salary range: $72,000 - $75,000 commensurate with experience. Benefits: TU offers a comprehensive benefits package that includes excellent health, life and retirement plans; and tuition remission. To learn more about our benefits, click here for regular faculty/regular lecturer or here for contingent lecturer. TU also offers a variety of great perks and discounts, which can be found here . Background Check: A Criminal Background Investigation is required for the hired candidate and the results may impact employment. COVID-19 Statement: The safety of our students, faculty, staff, and neighbors has been our top priority and the focus of every one of our decisions since the earliest days of the COVID-19 pandemic. Therefore, the University System of Maryland (USM) has strongly encouraged full COVID vaccination and up-to-date booster shots (when eligible) for all faculty, staff, and students at all schools in the USM as both a reasonable and necessary means of protecting our health and safety. Organization : Academic Affairs Division Primary Location : Main Campus Job Posting : Aug 18, 2026 Towson University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. If you need a reasonable accommodation for any part of the employment process, please send an email to: adarequest@towson.edu Towson University is a smoke-free campus. \u00a92016 | 8000 York Road | Towson, MD 21252 | 410-704-2000"}, "https://towson.taleo.net/careersection/fac_ex/jobdetail.ftl?job=260000P2": {"title": "Assistant Professor, African American History to 1900", "description": "Job Description - Assistant Professor, African American History to 1900 (260000P2) Go to the main content section. Welcome.  You are not signed in.  NOTE: If you experience any issues with this page, please contact the Towson University Office of Human Resources at 410-704-2162. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Assistant Professor, African American History to 1900 (260000P2) Job Description Assistant Professor, African American History to 1900 - ( 260000P2 ) TU Search Number : CLA-4021 Assistant Professor, African American History to 1900 Department of History College of Liberal Arts CLA-4021 Towson University: Towson University (TU) is one of the nation\u2019s top 100 public universities. Located north of Baltimore, TU currently enrolls over 19,000 students and is the second-largest university in the prestigious University System of Maryland. Towson University fosters a climate that is grounded in respect to cultivate the intellectual and personal growth of the entire university community. Position: The College of Liberal Arts invites applications for a tenure-track, 9-month position for an Assistant Professor of African American History in the Department of History. Preferred start date August 2027. Qualifications: PhD in History or related fields required. ABD applicants considered, but appointment will be at the \u2018Instructor\u2019 rank and all degree requirements must be completed by February 1, 2028. Research specialization in African American History from the Colonial Era to 1900 , all geographic areas of specialization are welcome. Demonstrated excellence in teaching in applicant\u2019s field of specialization. Demonstrated scholarship and active research agenda. Responsibilities: The successful candidate will be expected to teach and develop upper- and lower-level courses in African American History as well as in their other areas of specialization. Towson University and the Department of History are transitioning to the research-intensive R2 status, and candidates will be expected to contribute to this move and to pursue grant-based scholarship as outlined in the University\u2019s mission and strategic plan . The normal teaching load is 3-3, with a reduced 2-3 load for the first year. The successful candidate will commit to active participation and service to the department, college, and university. Application Process: Review of applications begins immediately and continues until the position is filled. Preliminary interviews will be conducted via Zoom, beginning in January 2027. Submit a letter of application, curriculum vitae, and contact information of three professional references. The letter of application should contain the following: a description of research and a description of one upper-division course and one lower-division course applicant would be prepared to teach. A writing sample, unofficial graduate transcripts, and letters of professional references will be requested from those candidates who advance to preliminary interviews. Contact Michael Masatsugu, Chair of Search Committee, (mmasatsugu@towson.edu) with any questions. Click here to apply. Please note that the search number for which you are applying is CLA-4021. Please be sure to visit the Applicant Data Form to complete a voluntary on-line form. All data collected are for internal, state, and/or federal reporting and will not be used for other purposes. Salary and Benefits: Targeted salary range: $72,000-75,000 commensurate with experience. Benefits: TU offers a comprehensive benefits package that includes excellent health, life and retirement plans; and tuition remission. To learn more about our benefits, click here for regular faculty/regular lecturer or here for contingent lecturer. TU also offers a variety of great perks and discounts, which can be found here . Background Check: A Criminal Background Investigation is required for the hired candidate and the results may impact employment. COVID-19 Statement: The safety of our students, faculty, staff, and neighbors has been our top priority and the focus of every one of our decisions since the earliest days of the COVID-19 pandemic. Therefore, the University System of Maryland (USM) has strongly encouraged full COVID vaccination and up-to-date booster shots (when eligible) for all faculty, staff, and students at all schools in the USM as both a reasonable and necessary means of protecting our health and safety. Organization : Academic Affairs Division Primary Location : Main Campus Job Posting : Sep 17, 2026 Towson University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. If you need a reasonable accommodation for any part of the employment process, please send an email to: adarequest@towson.edu Towson University is a smoke-free campus. \u00a92016 | 8000 York Road | Towson, MD 21252 | 410-704-2000"}, "https://towson.taleo.net/careersection/fac_ex/jobdetail.ftl?job=260000JA": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Political Science", "description": "Job Description - Assistant Professor of Political Science (260000JA) Go to the main content section. Welcome.  You are not signed in.  NOTE: If you experience any issues with this page, please contact the Towson University Office of Human Resources at 410-704-2162. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Assistant Professor of Political Science (260000JA) Job Description Assistant Professor of Political Science - ( 260000JA ) TU Search Number : CLA-4009 Assistant Professor Department of Political Science College of Liberal Arts CLA-4009 Towson University: Towson University (TU) is one of the nation\u2019s top 100 public universities. Located north of Baltimore, TU currently enrolls over 19,000 students and is the second-largest university in the prestigious University System of Maryland. Towson University fosters a climate that is grounded in respect to cultivate the intellectual and personal growth of the entire university community. Position: The College of Liberal Arts invites applications for an Assistant Professor position in the Political Science Department. Preferred start date August 2027. Qualifications: Applicants with a Ph.D. in hand will receive preference, although ABDs may be considered if the degree will be completed by the end of Spring 2027 Responsibilities: Areas of Specialization: Constitutional Law, Judicial Politics, Homeland Security The Department of Political Science invites applications for a tenure-track, 9-month position in Political Science with an emphasis in Constitutional Law. The position entails teaching a general undergraduate survey course on Law and Politics, upper-division courses in Constitutional Law and Judicial Politics, and a graduate course in Homeland Security and Constitutional Rights. The individual appointed will have the opportunity to develop future course offerings. Successful applicants will demonstrate both a commitment to teaching excellence and strong potential for a productive scholarly program. As the university nears the attainment of Carnegie\u2019s R2 status, candidates should also prioritize grant-funded research. Additional responsibilities include advising students in the major and minor, and service to the department, college, and university. Candidates must be sensitive to the needs of, and possess an interest in working with, a diverse student body. They should also consider how they would address the university\u2019s mission , strategic plan , and Presidential Priorities . Application Process: Review of applications begins immediately and continues until the position is filled. Interested applicants should submit the following: 1) letter of intent; 2) curriculum vitae; 3) one sample of written work; 4) a statement of teaching philosophy, plus syllabi and teaching evaluations if available; 5) graduate transcripts; and 6) names and addresses, including email addresses, of three (3) references. If selected for the short list, letters of reference will be thereby requested. Submit all application materials in a single PDF file to Taleo. Please direct questions about applications to: Dr. Paul T. McCartney (pmccartney@towson.edu) Click here to apply. Please note that the search number for which you are applying is CLA-4009. Please be sure to visit the Applicant Data Form to complete a voluntary on-line form. All data collected are for internal, state, and/or federal reporting and will not be used for other purposes. Salary and Benefits: Targeted salary range: $70,000 - $75,000 commensurate with experience. Benefits: TU offers a comprehensive benefits package that includes excellent health, life and retirement plans; and tuition remission. To learn more about our benefits, click here for regular faculty/regular lecturer or here for contingent lecturer. TU also offers a variety of great perks and discounts, which can be found here . Background Check: A Criminal Background Investigation is required for the hired candidate, and the results may impact employment. COVID-19 Statement: The safety of our students, faculty, staff, and neighbors has been our top priority and the focus of every one of our decisions since the earliest days of the COVID-19 pandemic. Therefore, the University System of Maryland (USM) has strongly encouraged full COVID vaccination and up-to-date booster shots (when eligible) for all faculty, staff, and students at all schools in the USM as both a reasonable and necessary means of protecting our health and safety. Organization : Academic Affairs Division Primary Location : Main Campus Job Posting : Jul 16, 2026 Towson University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. If you need a reasonable accommodation for any part of the employment process, please send an email to: adarequest@towson.edu Towson University is a smoke-free campus. \u00a92016 | 8000 York Road | Towson, MD 21252 | 410-704-2000"}, "https://towson.taleo.net/careersection/fac_ex/jobdetail.ftl?job=260000I9": {"title": "Assistant Professor, Ecology/Evolution", "description": "Job Description - Assistant Professor, Ecology/Evolution (260000I9) Go to the main content section. Welcome.  You are not signed in.  NOTE: If you experience any issues with this page, please contact the Towson University Office of Human Resources at 410-704-2162. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Assistant Professor, Ecology/Evolution (260000I9) Job Description Assistant Professor, Ecology/Evolution - ( 260000I9 ) TU Search Number : FCSM-4001 Assistant Professor, Ecology/Evolution Department of Biological Sciences The Jess and Mildred Fisher College of Science & Mathematics FCSM-4001 Towson University : Towson University (TU) is one of the nation\u2019s top 100 public universities. Located north of Baltimore, TU currently enrolls over 19,000 students and is the second-largest university in the prestigious University System of Maryland. Towson University fosters a climate that is grounded in respect to cultivate the intellectual and personal growth of the entire university community. Position: The Jess and Mildred Fisher College of Science & Mathematics invites applications for a full-time, tenure track, 9-month Assistant Professor position in the Department of Biological Sciences. Preferred start date is August 2027. Qualifications: Successful applicants are expected to possess a strong commitment to excellence in teaching, to establish a productive research/scholarly program involving undergraduate and Master\u2019s level graduate students, and to actively pursue extramural funding for that research. Successful candidates are required to have a Ph.D. in the biological sciences or related field and have postdoctoral experience. Responsibilities: The candidate will primarily teach introductory-level undergraduate biology and upper-level courses in evolution, conservation biology, or ecology, but may also teach undergraduate and graduate courses aligned with the candidate\u2019s area(s) of expertise. The candidate must establish a competitive research program that engages undergraduate students in biology and/or other related majors. The successful candidate\u2019s research program should focus on plant or algal biology, lichenology, or mycology, and may be conducted at any scale from the organismal to the ecosystem level. The candidate is expected to pursue external research funding and disseminate their research findings in peer-reviewed journals and through presentations at professional meetings. Pre-tenure faculty members are assigned an instructional workload of five (5) course units per academic year. The Department: The Department of Biological Sciences provides high-quality education to both undergraduate and graduate students, with a focus on the knowledge and skills necessary for success at Towson University and beyond. The department enrolls ~1000 undergraduates in biology, as well as ~40 graduate students in the biology master\u2019s program. The department supports interdisciplinary programs in molecular biology, biochemistry and bioinformatics (MBBB), environmental science, and animal behavior, as well as service courses in the College of Health Professions. Application Process: Review of applications begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Incomplete applications will not be considered. To apply, please upload a\u202fsingle\u202fpdf file\u202fcontaining the following documents in the specified order: 1. A cover letter stating your interest in the position and your potential contributions to the undergraduate biology program at Towson University. (1 page limit) 2.\u202fA current curriculum vitae highlighting relevant teaching experience. (3 page limit) 3.\u202fA statement of teaching philosophy that specifically addresses your approach to teaching undergraduate lecture and lab. (2 page limit) 4. A description of your proposed research program at Towson University. You must include at least two different projects, and describe how they are appropriate for undergraduate student researchers. (4 page limit, including references). 5.\u202fNames and contact information (current affiliation, e-mail address and telephone number) for three professional references. 6.\u202fCopies of all graduate and undergraduate transcripts (listed in reverse chronological order). Application Process: Review of applications begins immediately and continues until the position is filled. Applicants must submit these materials electronically through Towson University's internal application system, TALEO. Click here to apply. P lease note that the search number for which you are applying is FCSM-4001. Please, be sure to visit the Applicant Data Form to complete a voluntary on-line form. All data collected\u00a0are\u00a0for internal, state, and/or federal reporting and will not be used for other purposes. Please address any questions regarding the position or the search to the search committee chair: Dr. Harald Beck ( hbeck@towson.edu ). Salary and Benefits: Targeted salary range: $79,000-$83,000, commensurate with experience. Benefits: TU offers a comprehensive benefits package that includes excellent health, life and retirement plans, and tuition remission. To learn more about our benefits, click here . For regular faculty/teaching professor or here for contingent teaching professor. TU also offers a variety of great\u00a0perks\u00a0and discounts, which can be found here . Background Check: A Criminal Background Investigation is\u00a0required\u00a0for the hired\u00a0candidate\u00a0and the results ay\u00a0impact\u00a0employment. COVID-19 Statement: The safety of our students, faculty, staff, and neighbors has been our top priority and the focus of every one of our decisions since the earliest days of the COVID-19 pandemic. Therefore, the University System of Maryland (USM) has strongly encouraged full COVID vaccination and up-to-date booster shots (when eligible) for all faculty, staff, and students at all schools in the USM as both a reasonable and necessary means of protecting our health and safety. Organization : Academic Affairs Division Primary Location : Main Campus Job Posting : Jul 3, 2026 Towson University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. If you need a reasonable accommodation for any part of the employment process, please send an email to: adarequest@towson.edu Towson University is a smoke-free campus. \u00a92016 | 8000 York Road | Towson, MD 21252 | 410-704-2000"}, "https://towson.taleo.net/careersection/fac_ex/jobdetail.ftl?job=260000I3": {"title": "Assistant Professor \u2013 Cell/Molecular Biology", "description": "Job Description - Assistant Professor \u2013 Cell/Molecular Biology (260000I3) Go to the main content section. Welcome.  You are not signed in.  NOTE: If you experience any issues with this page, please contact the Towson University Office of Human Resources at 410-704-2162. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Assistant Professor \u2013 Cell/Molecular Biology (260000I3) Job Description Assistant Professor \u2013 Cell/Molecular Biology - ( 260000I3 ) TU Search Number : FCSM-4002 Assistant Professor \u2013 Cell/Molecular Biology Department of Biological Sciences The Jess and Mildred Fisher College of Science & Mathematics FCSM-4002 Towson University : Towson University (TU) is one of the nation\u2019s top 100 public universities. Located north of Baltimore, TU currently enrolls over 19,000 students and is the second-largest university in the prestigious University System of Maryland. Towson University fosters a climate that is grounded in respect to cultivate the intellectual and personal growth of the entire university community. Position : The Jess and Mildred Fisher College of Science & Mathematics invites applications for a full-time, tenure track, 9-month Assistant Professor position in the Department of Biological Sciences. Preferred start date is August 2027. Qualifications : Successful applicants are expected to possess a strong commitment to excellence in teaching, to establish a productive research/scholarly program involving undergraduate and Master\u2019s level graduate students, and to actively pursue extramural funding for that research. Successful candidates are required to have a PhD in the biological sciences or related field, and have postdoctoral experience. Responsibilities : The candidate will primarily teach undergraduate lecture and lab courses in Introduction to Cell/Molecular Biology, Genetics, and/or Microbiology, but may also teach other undergraduate and graduate courses in Cell/Molecular Biology that align with faculty area(s) of expertise. The candidate must establish a competitive research program that engages undergraduate students in biology and/or other related majors. The candidate is expected to pursue external research funding and disseminate their research findings in peer-reviewed journals and through presentations at professional meetings. Pre-tenure faculty members are assigned an instructional workload of five (5) course units per academic year. The Department: The Department of Biological Sciences provides high-quality education to both undergraduate and graduate students, with a focus on the knowledge and skills necessary for success at Towson University and beyond. The department enrolls ~1000 undergraduates in biology, as well as ~40 graduate students in the biology master\u2019s program. The department supports interdisciplinary programs in molecular biology, biochemistry and bioinformatics (MBBB), environmental science, and animal behavior, as well as service courses in the College of Health Professions. Application Process: Review of applications begin immediately and will continue until the positions are filled. Incomplete applications will not be considered. To apply, please upload a\u202fsingle\u202fpdf file\u202fcontaining the following documents in the specified order: 1. A cover letter stating your interest in the position and your potential contributions to the undergraduate biology program at Towson University. (1 page limit) 2.\u202fA current curriculum vitae highlighting relevant teaching experience. (3 page limit) 3.\u202fA statement of teaching philosophy that specifically addresses your approach to teaching undergraduate lecture and lab. (2 page limit) 4. A description of your proposed research program at Towson University. You must include at least two different projects, and describe how they are appropriate for undergraduate student researchers. (4 page limit, including references). 5.\u202fNames and contact information (current affiliation, e-mail address and telephone number) for three professional references. 6.\u202fCopies of all graduate and undergraduate transcripts (listed in reverse chronological order). Application Process: Review of applications begins immediately and continues until the position is filled. Applicants must submit these materials electronically through Towson University's internal application system, TALEO. Click here to apply. P lease note that the search number for which you are applying is FCSM-4002. Please, be sure to visit the Applicant Data Form to complete a voluntary on-line form. All data collected\u00a0are\u00a0for internal, state, and/or federal reporting and will not be used for other purposes. Please address any questions regarding the position or the search to the search committee chair: Dr. Peko Tsuji ( ptsuji@towson.edu ). Salary and Benefits: Targeted salary range: $79,000-$83,000, commensurate with experience. Benefits: TU offers a comprehensive benefits package that includes excellent health, life and retirement plans, and tuition remission. To learn more about our benefits, click here . For regular faculty/teaching professor or here for contingent teaching professor. TU also offers a variety of great\u00a0perks\u00a0and discounts, which can be found here . Background Check: A Criminal Background Investigation is\u00a0required\u00a0for the hired\u00a0candidate\u00a0and the results may\u00a0impact\u00a0employment. COVID-19 Statement: The safety of our students, faculty, staff, and neighbors has been our top priority and the focus of every one of our decisions since the earliest days of the COVID-19 pandemic. Therefore, the University System of Maryland (USM) has strongly encouraged full COVID vaccination and up-to-date booster shots (when eligible) for all faculty, staff, and students at all schools in the USM as both a reasonable and necessary means of protecting our health and safety. Organization : Academic Affairs Division Primary Location : Main Campus Job Posting : Jul 2, 2026 Towson University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. If you need a reasonable accommodation for any part of the employment process, please send an email to: adarequest@towson.edu Towson University is a smoke-free campus. \u00a92016 | 8000 York Road | Towson, MD 21252 | 410-704-2000"}, "https://towson.taleo.net/careersection/fac_ex/jobdetail.ftl?job=260000IF": {"title": "Assistant Professor, Organic Chemistry", "description": "Job Description - Assistant Professor, Organic Chemistry (260000IF) Go to the main content section. Welcome.  You are not signed in.  NOTE: If you experience any issues with this page, please contact the Towson University Office of Human Resources at 410-704-2162. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Assistant Professor, Organic Chemistry (260000IF) Job Description Assistant Professor, Organic Chemistry - ( 260000IF ) TU Search Number : FCSM-4008 Assistant Professor, Organic Chemistry Department of Chemistry & Forensic Science The Jess and Mildred Fisher College of Science and Mathematics FCSM-4008 Towson University: Towson University (TU) is one of the nation\u2019s top 100 public universities. Located north of Baltimore, TU currently enrolls over 19,000 students and is the second-largest university in the prestigious University System of Maryland. Towson University fosters a climate that is grounded in respect to cultivate the intellectual and personal growth of the entire university community. Position: The Jess and Mildred Fisher College of Science and Mathematics invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor in Organic Chemistry position in the Department of Chemistry & Forensic Science. Preferred start date, August 2027. Qualifications: A Ph.D. in organic chemistry is required. Postdoctoral research and experience teaching undergraduates is strongly preferred. The department is particularly interested in candidates whose proposed research program will complement existing departmental strengths in target-directed synthesis; however, candidates in all areas of organic chemistry will receive full consideration. Responsibilities: The candidate will primarily teach undergraduate lecture and lab courses in organic chemistry but may also teach courses in the general chemistry sequence and upper-division courses in their area of expertise. The candidate must establish a competitive research program that engages undergraduate students in chemistry, forensic chemistry, and other related majors. The candidate is expected to pursue external research funding and disseminate their research findings in peer-reviewed journals and through presentations at professional meetings. Pre-tenure faculty members are assigned an instructional workload of five (5) course units per academic year. The Department: The Department of Chemistry & Forensic Science is ACS accredited, with 17 tenured or tenure-track faculty actively engaged in externally funded research involving undergraduates and graduate students. The department enrolls approximately 300 undergraduates in chemistry, forensic chemistry and chemistry secondary education, and 40 graduate students in the forensic science master\u2019s program. The department supports interdisciplinary programs in molecular biology, biochemistry and bioinformatics (MB3), and environmental science. Additional collaborative opportunities may be available with science faculty in the departments of anthropology, biology, computer sciences, mathematics, and physics, astronomy & geosciences. The department also features state-of-the-art instrumentation to support undergraduate research, including a new 400 MHz NMR spectrometer. Application Process : Review of applications begins on September 1, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. Incomplete applications and applications received after September 1, 2026 may not be reviewed by the search committee. To apply, please upload a single pdf file containing the following documents in the specified order: 1. \u00a0A cover letter stating your interest in the position and your potential contributions to the undergraduate chemistry program at Towson University. (1 page limit) 2. \u00a0 A current curriculum vitae highlighting relevant teaching and research experience. (3 page limit) 3. A statement of teaching philosophy that specifically addresses your approach to teaching undergraduate organic chemistry lecture and lab. (2 page limit) 4. A description of your proposed research program at Towson University. You must include at least two different projects and describe how they are appropriate for undergraduate student researchers. (4 page limit, including references). 5. Names and contact information (current affiliation, e-mail address, and telephone number) for three professional references. 6. Copies of all graduate and undergraduate transcripts (listed in reverse chronological order). Click on the link below to apply. Please note that the search number for which you are applying is FCSM-4008. Please be sure to visit the Applicant Data Form to complete a voluntary on-line form. All data collected are for internal, state, and/or federal reporting and will not be used for other purposes. For more information, please contact the chair of the search committee, Dr. Keith Reber, at organicsearch2026@towson.edu. Salary and Benefits: Targeted salary range: $77,000 \u2013 $81,000, commensurate with experience. Benefits: TU offers a comprehensive benefits package that includes excellent health, life and retirement plans, and tuition remission. To learn more about our benefits, click here for regular faculty/regular lecturer or here for contingent lecturer. TU also offers a variety of great perks and discounts, which can be found here . Background Check: A Criminal Background Investigation is required for the hired candidate, and the results may impact employment. COVID-19 Statement: The safety of our students, faculty, staff, and neighbors has been our top priority and the focus of every one of our decisions since the earliest days of the COVID-19 pandemic. Therefore, the University System of Maryland (USM) has strongly encouraged full COVID vaccination and up-to-date booster shots (when eligible) for all faculty, staff, and students at all schools in the USM as both a reasonable and necessary means of protecting our health and safety. Organization : Academic Affairs Division Primary Location : Main Campus Job Posting : Jul 7, 2026 Towson University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. If you need a reasonable accommodation for any part of the employment process, please send an email to: adarequest@towson.edu Towson University is a smoke-free campus. \u00a92016 | 8000 York Road | Towson, MD 21252 | 410-704-2000"}, "https://towson.taleo.net/careersection/fac_ex/jobdetail.ftl?job=260000JI": {"title": "Assistant Professor, Forensic Chemistry", "description": "Job Description - Assistant Professor, Forensic Chemistry (260000JI) Go to the main content section. Welcome.  You are not signed in.  NOTE: If you experience any issues with this page, please contact the Towson University Office of Human Resources at 410-704-2162. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Assistant Professor, Forensic Chemistry (260000JI) Job Description Assistant Professor, Forensic Chemistry - ( 260000JI ) TU Search Number : FCSM-4011 Assistant Professor, Forensic Chemistry Department of Chemistry & Forensic Science The Jess and Mildred Fisher College of Science and Mathematics FCSM-4011 Towson University: Towson University (TU) is one of the nation\u2019s top 100 public universities. Located north of Baltimore, TU currently enrolls over 19,000 students and is the second-largest university in the prestigious University System of Maryland. Towson University fosters a climate that is grounded in respect to cultivate the intellectual and personal growth of the entire university community. Position: The Jess and Mildred Fisher College of Science and Mathematics invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor in a Forensic Chemistry position in the Department of Chemistry & Forensic Science. Preferred begin date, August 2027. Priority in this search will be given to candidates who can support teaching and research in our forensic programs at the nexus of forensic chemistry and analytical chemistry. Qualifications: A Ph.D. in analytical chemistry or forensic chemistry is required. Postdoctoral research in analytical and/or forensic chemistry, experience in a forensic trace, forensic drug, or forensic toxicology laboratory, and experience teaching undergraduates and graduate students is strongly preferred. The department is particularly interested in candidates whose proposed research and teaching will complement existing departmental strengths in forensic chemistry and analytical chemistry. Responsibilities: The candidate will primarily teach lecture and lab courses in the Master of Science in Forensic Science (MSFS) and in the forensic chemistry undergraduate programs. Candidates may also teach other courses depending on departmental needs. The candidate must establish a competitive independent research program that engages undergraduate and graduate students in forensic chemistry. The candidate is expected to pursue external research funding and disseminate their research findings in peer-reviewed journals and through presentations at professional meetings. Pre-tenure faculty members are assigned an instructional workload of five (5) course units per academic year. The Department: The Department of Chemistry & Forensic Science is ACS accredited, with 18 tenured or tenure-track faculty actively engaged in externally funded research involving undergraduates and graduate students. The department enrolls approximately 300 undergraduates in chemistry, forensic chemistry and chemistry secondary education, and 40 graduate students in the forensic science master\u2019s program. The department supports interdisciplinary programs in molecular biology, biochemistry and bioinformatics (MB3), and environmental science. Additional collaborative opportunities may be available with science faculty in the departments of anthropology, biology, computer sciences, mathematics, and physics, astronomy & geosciences. Application Process : Review of applications begins on September 1, 2026 , and will continue until the position is filled. Incomplete applications and applications received after September 1, 2026, will not be reviewed by the search committee. To apply, please upload a single pdf file to Taleo containing the following documents in the specified order: 1. A cover letter stating your interest in the position and your potential contributions to the Master of Science in Forensic Science and Bachelor of Science in Forensic Chemistry programs at Towson University. (1 page limit) 2. A current curriculum vitae highlighting relevant teaching and research experience. (3-page limit) 3. A statement of teaching philosophy that specifically addresses your approach to teaching master's and undergraduate level lectures and labs. (1 page limit) 4. A description of your proposed research program at Towson University. You must include at least two different projects and describe how they are appropriate for graduate and undergraduate students in our Forensic Science Education Programs Accreditation Commission (FEPAC) Accredited programs. Emphasis on research with MSFS students is required (4-page limit, including references). 5. Official copies of all graduate and undergraduate transcripts (listed in reverse chronological order). Additionally, candidates must arrange for three confidential letters of recommendation to be sent to FRSCsearch@towson.edu by 5:00 PM Eastern time on August 30 th , 2026 . Letters must focus on the candidate\u2019s ability to establish an independent research program in forensic analytical chemistry (trace, drug, or toxicology), current research productivity, and ability to teach and work as part of a team. Click here to apply. Please note that the search number for which you are applying is FCSM-4011. Please be sure to visit the Applicant Data Form to complete a voluntary on-line form. All data collected are for internal, state, and/or federal reporting and will not be used for other purposes. For more information, please contact the chair of the search committee, Dr. Ellen Hondrogiannis, at FRSCsearch@towson.edu. Salary and Benefits: Targeted salary range: $77,000 \u2013 $81,000, commensurate with experience. Benefits: TU offers a comprehensive benefits package that includes excellent health, life and retirement plans, and tuition remission. To learn more about our benefits, click here for regular faculty/regular lecturer or here for contingent lecturer. TU also offers a variety of great perks and discounts, which can be found here . Background Check: A Criminal Background Investigation is required for the hired candidate, and the results may impact employment. COVID-19 Statement: The safety of our students, faculty, staff, and neighbors has been our top priority and the focus of every one of our decisions since the earliest days of the COVID-19 pandemic. Therefore, the University System of Maryland (USM) has strongly encouraged full COVID vaccination and up- to-date booster shots (when eligible) for all faculty, staff, and students at all schools in the USM as both a reasonable and necessary means of protecting our health and safety. Organization : Academic Affairs Division Primary Location : Main Campus Job Posting : Jul 17, 2026 Towson University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. If you need a reasonable accommodation for any part of the employment process, please send an email to: adarequest@towson.edu Towson University is a smoke-free campus. \u00a92016 | 8000 York Road | Towson, MD 21252 | 410-704-2000"}, "https://towson.taleo.net/careersection/fac_ex/jobdetail.ftl?job=260000QQ": {"title": "Asst Prof - Math Education", "description": "Job Description - Asst Prof - Math Education (260000QQ) Go to the main content section. Welcome.  You are not signed in.  NOTE: If you experience any issues with this page, please contact the Towson University Office of Human Resources at 410-704-2162. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Asst Prof - Math Education (260000QQ) Job Description Asst Prof - Math Education - ( 260000QQ ) TU Search Number : FCSM-4026 Assistant Professor \u2013 Mathematics Education Department of Mathematics The Jess and Mildred Fisher College of Science and Mathematics FCSM-4026 Towson University : Towson University (TU) is one of the nation\u2019s top 100 public universities. Located north of Baltimore, TU currently enrolls over 20,000 students and is the second-largest university in the prestigious University System of Maryland. Towson University fosters a climate that is grounded in respect to cultivate the intellectual and personal growth of the entire university community. Position: The Fisher College of Science and Mathematics invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Mathematics Education position in the Mathematics Department. Preferred start date August 2027. Qualifications: Candidates must possess a Ph.D. (or equivalent) in Mathematics Education, Mathematics (with significant work experience in Mathematics Education), Curriculum and Instruction (with focus in Mathematics Education), or a closely related field, before August 15, 2027. Candidates should have a strong research background, potential for external funding, and excellent teaching. Candidates in all mathematics education specialties (including elementary, middle school, secondary, and undergraduate mathematics education) are encouraged to apply. Responsibilities: Assistant Professors are assigned an instructional workload of five course units (three credit hours each) per academic year. Faculty members in mathematics education teach a broad spectrum of courses throughout the undergraduate curriculum and in the Master\u2019s degree program in Mathematics Education. A strong commitment to excellence in teaching is essential. The successful candidate will establish a productive research program with a willingness to pursue external funding opportunities. The department is strongly committed to teacher preparation and undergraduate research. The Department : The Department of Mathematics has 58 full-time faculty and over 130 math majors. We offer a Bachelor of Science degree in mathematics, with concentrations in Secondary Education, Actuarial Science, Applied Mathematics, and Pure Mathematics, as well as Master\u2019s degrees in Mathematics Education, Actuarial Science and Predictive Analytics, and Applied and Industrial Mathematics. The Secondary Education concentration is offered in partnership with Towson UTeach, Maryland\u2019s leader in STEM teacher education. Application Process: Review of applications begins immediately and continues until the position is filled. Applications received prior to December 1, 2026 will receive full consideration. Applications should be submitted electronically through www.mathjobs.org. A complete application includes a cover letter, curriculum vitae, all graduate transcripts, a research statement, a teaching statement, and at least three recommendation letters, one of which should address the candidate\u2019s teaching. In addition, candidates must upload their CV through Towson University's internal application system, Taleo, using the following link: Click here to apply. Please note that the search number for which you are applying is FCSM-4026. Please be sure to visit the Applicant Data Form to complete a voluntary on-line form. All data collected are for internal, state, and/or federal reporting and will not be used for other purposes. Salary and Benefits: Targeted salary range: $76,000-$80,000 commensurate with experience. Benefits: TU offers a comprehensive benefits package that includes excellent health, life and retirement plans; and tuition remission. To learn more about our benefits, click here for regular faculty/regular lecturer or here for contingent lecturer. TU also offers a variety of great perks and discounts, which can be found here . Background Check: A criminal background investigation is required for the successful candidate, and results may affect employment. COVID-19 Statement: The safety of our students, faculty, staff, and neighbors has been our top priority and the focus of every one of our decisions since the earliest days of the COVID-19 pandemic. Therefore, the University System of Maryland (USM) has strongly encouraged full COVID vaccination and up-to-date booster shots (when eligible) for all faculty, staff, and students at all schools in the USM as both a reasonable and necessary means of protecting our health and safety. Organization : Academic Affairs Division Primary Location : Main Campus Job Posting : Sep 28, 2026 Towson University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. If you need a reasonable accommodation for any part of the employment process, please send an email to: adarequest@towson.edu Towson University is a smoke-free campus. \u00a92016 | 8000 York Road | Towson, MD 21252 | 410-704-2000"}}, "rows": {"https://towson.taleo.net/careersection/fac_ex/jobdetail.ftl?job=260000JS": {"school_id": 609, "posting_url": "https://towson.taleo.net/careersection/fac_ex/jobdetail.ftl?job=260000JS", "job_title_in_post": "Collection Management Librarian", "position_type": "Non-academic", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": "November 4, 2026"}, "https://towson.taleo.net/careersection/fac_ex/jobdetail.ftl?job=260000OM": {"school_id": 609, "posting_url": "https://towson.taleo.net/careersection/fac_ex/jobdetail.ftl?job=260000OM", "job_title_in_post": "Assistant Professor in Finance", "position_type": "Assistant_Professor", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "Finance", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://towson.taleo.net/careersection/fac_ex/jobdetail.ftl?job=260000N7": {"school_id": 609, "postin